    content: "# Astris Travel \342\200\224 Implementation Plan\n\nAstris Travel is a split-screen multi-destination travel planning and route optimization workspace that pairs an interactive drag-and-drop itinerary timeline with a synchronized geodesic world map, multi-modal transit comparison, Smart Score ranking, two-stage route optimization, and automatic voucher matching.\n\n---\n\n### User Review & Critical Decisions\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> All core architectural choices below incorporate your Phase 1 answers and govern how the live preview, mapping engine, and shared data contracts are structured.\n\n- **Confirmed Decision 1 \342\200\224 Hybrid Live Runtime + FastAPI Schemas**: Build a live, immediately previewable React + Vite + Express TypeScript application on port 3000 while also delivering the shared TypeScript contracts and Python FastAPI + Pydantic v2 models (`Trip`, `TripLeg`, `TransitOption`, `Voucher`) alongside the structured JSON mock dataset.\n- **Confirmed Decision 2 \342\200\224 Token-Free MapLibre GL**: Use `react-map-gl` (MapLibre entrypoint) paired with `maplibre-gl` and `@turf/great-circle` over a clean, token-free Carto Positron vector/raster basemap so numbered destination pins and curved geodesic flight arcs render reliably with zero API key friction.\n- **Confirmed Decision 3 \342\200\224 Full Interactive Workspace**: Ship the complete split-screen workspace upfront, including drag-and-drop stop reordering, adding/removing destinations, live Smart Score recalculation, two-stage route optimization, and interactive voucher application.\n- **Confirmed Decision 4 \342\200\224 Mock Dataset + Express API Endpoints First**: Back the interactive client with Express `/api/*` endpoints serving and evaluating the realistic 4-stop `Kuala Lumpur \342\206\222 Istanbul \342\206\222 London \342\206\222 Paris` dataset (plus expandable global hubs), keeping persistence lightweight before connecting live transit feeds or PostgreSQL.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Overview & Core Concept\n\n- **What It Does**: Users build and refine multi-city international itineraries in a synchronized split-screen workspace. Reordering or adding stops on the left timeline immediately updates numbered pins and great-circle flight arcs on the right map, queries multi-modal door-to-door transit options (flights, high-speed rail, and intercity coaches), ranks them via the Smart Score formula, applies eligible promo vouchers, and runs a two-stage geographical + transit optimizer to suggest better stop sequences.\n- **Target Audience / Persona**: Global travelers, digital nomads, and multi-leg trip planners balancing ticket cost against travel and layover hours across air and ground transport.\n- **Key Value**: Eliminates multi-tab spreadsheet planning by quantifying the true time-adjusted cost of every leg (`Price + (Travel & Layover Hours \303\227 Hourly Time Value)`) and immediately visualizing route geometry and savings on one canvas.\n\n---\n\n### 2. User Experience & Visual Design\n\n- **Key User Flows**:\n  1. **Initial Workspace Load**: Opens directly into the pre-loaded 4-stop trip (`1. Kuala Lumpur \342\206\222 2. Istanbul \342\206\222 3. London \342\206\222 4. Paris`), displaying total trip cost, total travel hours, active Smart Score hourly valuation (`$45/hr` default), and numbered geodesic arcs across Asia and Europe.\n  2. **Timeline & Map Synchronization**: Users drag stops by their grip handle to reorder the sequence, hover over any stop or leg to highlight its corresponding pin and curved arc on the map, click a leg to inspect door-to-door flight/train/bus alternatives, or add/remove stops from a searchable destination picker.\n  3. **Smart Score & Multi-Modal Filtering**: Adjusting the **Time Value (`$/hr`)** slider or toggling the floating glassmorphic transport filter bar (`All`, `Flight`, `Train`, `Bus`) over the map dynamically recalculates Smart Scores and re-ranks transit cards in real time.\n  4. **Two-Stage Route Optimizer**: Clicking **Optimize Route** in the top bar runs Stage 1 (local geographical permutation scoring via Haversine/great-circle distance) and Stage 2 (Express API transit evaluation of top paths), presenting a comparison drawer with net distance, hours, and cost deltas that can be applied in one click.\n  5. **Voucher & Promo Matching**: Users enter a promo code or toggle matched eligible vouchers on a selected transit option; the engine validates corridor, mode, carrier, and minimum spend rules, updating the net fare and Smart Score inline.\n\n- **Visual Identity & Theme**:\n  - *Aesthetic Direction*: Modern, airy travel-tech workspace blending editorial clarity with high-precision SaaS utility (Airbnb warmth meets Wanderlog spatial structure).\n  - *Color Palette & Mood*:\n    - **60% Dominant Neutral Canvas**: Crisp white (`#FFFFFF`) panels and soft slate-tinted workspace canvas (`bg-slate-50`).\n    - **30% Structural Surfaces**: Deep midnight slate typography (`text-slate-900` primary, `text-slate-600` secondary, `text-slate-500` metadata) and hairline borders (`border-slate-200/80`).\n    - **10% Accent Budget**: Electric indigo (`bg-indigo-600 hover:bg-indigo-700 text-white`, `text-indigo-600`) reserved strictly for primary CTAs, active route highlights, numbered map pins, and selected transit states.\n    - **Semantic Status**: Green (`#16A34A`) for savings/applied vouchers, Amber (`#D97706`) for long layovers, Crimson (`#DC2626`) for invalid vouchers or warnings\342\200\224always paired with explicit text labels.\n  - *Typography & Hierarchy*:\n    - Display & Headings: `Plus Jakarta Sans` (SemiBold/Bold) with `text-wrap: balance` on titles.\n    - Body & Controls: `DM Sans` (Regular/Medium) at 13px\342\200\22315px for crisp legibility.\n    - Numeric Telemetry: `JetBrains Mono` with `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` for fares, Smart Scores, durations, coordinates, and promo codes.\n  - *Component Styling & Layout*:\n    - **Top Bar Contract**: Clean single-row header with three zones (`Astris Travel` wordmark \342\200\224 concise workspace section links \342\200\224 single `Optimize Route` primary CTA).\n    - **Split-Screen Master Layout**: Full-viewport `1440px` desktop split (`46%` scrollable itinerary & transit inspector on the left, `54%` sticky interactive MapLibre canvas on the right, responsive stacked toggle on mobile).\n    - **Card & Metadata Restraint**: Single-elevation `rounded-2xl` cards (`border border-slate-200/80 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md`), clean unboxed metadata joined by typographic separators (`\302\267`, `/`), and zero nested card-in-card clutter or thick left accent borders.\n    - **Glassmorphic Map Controls**: Floating segmented transport filter bar (`All`, `Flight`, `Train`, `Bus`) and leg summary overlay positioned over the map using `bg-white/80 backdrop-blur-md border border-white/20 shadow-lg rounded-full`.\n\n- **Interactive Feedback & Motion**:\n  - Smooth 150\342\200\223200ms transitions (`cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)`) using `transform` and `opacity` during drag sorting, leg expansion, and map camera `flyTo` transitions.\n  - Complete empty state (when fewer than 2 stops remain), loading skeleton state during route optimization, and non-blocking inline error/validation feedback for promo codes.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Product Decisions & Trade-Offs\n\n- **Decision 1 \342\200\224 Live Express + React Architecture Alongside FastAPI/Pydantic Blueprint**:\n  - *Chosen Approach*: Serve the interactive React frontend and REST endpoints from a unified Express + Vite Node server on port 3000, while placing clean, production-ready Python FastAPI + Pydantic v2 model definitions and router specs in a dedicated backend reference module.\n  - *Why*: Ensures the application launches and runs live immediately in the preview environment without requiring a separate Python ASGI runtime, while honoring the exact Pydantic v2 data contracts needed for future Python microservice deployment.\n  - *Alternatives Considered*: A static Next.js + FastAPI folder scaffold was passed over because it would leave the port-3000 preview non-functional.\n\n- **Decision 2 \342\200\224 MapLibre GL (`react-map-gl/maplibre`) + `@turf/great-circle`**:\n  - *Chosen Approach*: Render the interactive world map with MapLibre GL and free Carto Positron vector/raster styles, drawing smooth spherical great-circle GeoJSON lines and custom HTML numbered markers.\n  - *Why*: Delivers smooth pan/zoom, `flyTo` synchronization, and crisp curved arcs immediately with zero access-token failures.\n  - *Alternatives Considered*: Raw Mapbox GL requires a private token that breaks in tokenless previews; static SVG maps lack real zoom/pan exploration.\n\n- **Decision 3 \342\200\224 Real-Time Client + Server Smart Score & Two-Stage Optimizer**:\n  - *Chosen Approach*: Compute interactive Smart Score slider updates instantaneously in client state for zero-latency scrubbing, while routing Two-Stage Route Optimization and Voucher Validation through dedicated Express `/api/*` endpoints.\n  - *Why*: Gives instant feedback when sliding Hourly Time Value while keeping route-permutation search and promo eligibility cleanly encapsulated in backend APIs.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Technical Architecture & Data Strategy *(Technical Reference)*\n\n- **Architecture & Component Diagram**:\n\n```\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202                         Top Navigation Bar (3 Zones)                      \342\224\202\n\342\224\202   Astris Travel   \342\224\202   Timeline \302\267 Smart Score \302\267 Vouchers   \342\224\202 Optimize Route\342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n                                      \342\224\202\n        \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\264\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\2