  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Revising Implementation Plan**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently focused on incorporating the user\'s brand identity. I\'m updating `implementation_plan.md` right now to feature Sunset Orange (`#FF812E`) and Crisp White. I\'m specifically looking at lines 35-58, which is my main focus. I am currently reading through lines 36-52.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Framework**\n\nNow I\'m fleshing out the visual framework. I am structuring the color palette with a modern aesthetic, aiming for a blend of clarity and utility. I\'m focusing on the dominant neutral canvas, structural surfaces, and accent colors to ensure an intuitive user experience. I\'m prioritizing semantic color status indicators to guide the user. I have started considering the typography.\n\n\n**Refining Typography & Layout**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on typographic details and component styling. For titles, I\'m leaning toward a font stack of `Roboto Sans` (SemiBold/Bold) with `text-wrap: balance`. Body and controls will use `DM Sans` (Regular/Medium) at 13-15px. Numeric telemetry will be `JetBrains Mono` with tabular numbers. I\'m also finalizing layout decisions, like the top bar contract and split-screen master layout. I am focused on clean cards and unboxed metadata and minimal nesting. Lastly, I\'m working on glassmorphic map controls.\n\n\n**Specifying UI Enhancements**\n\nI\'m currently designing the map overlay components. The leg summary and bar will now use a white background with 80% opacity and a backdrop blur, complemented by a white border, shadow, and rounded corners. I am also working on updating the map pin color to Sunset Orange with a soft white halo, and adding active geodesic arcs. I\'m also ensuring WCAG AA contrast for text, using `#FF812E` for the hero color, with a focus on accessible button design and color pairings like orange with white/dark gray.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_16569227233513494232"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Update Color Palette, Component Styling, and Map Styling in implementation_plan.md to use Sunset Orange (#FF812E) and Crisp White brand identity.\", \"EndLine\":55, \"Instruction\":\"Replace Indigo color palette and glassmorphism specs with Sunset Orange (#FF812E), Crisp White (#FFFFFF), Warm Neutral (#FAFAFA), Deep Charcoal (#111827), and Map Pin/Arc styling.\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"- **Visual Identity & Theme**:\\n  - *Aesthetic Direction*: Modern, airy travel-tech workspace blending editorial clarity with high-precision SaaS utility (Airbnb warmth meets Wanderlog spatial structure).\\n  - *Color Palette & Mood*:\\n    - **60% Dominant Neutral Canvas**: Pure crisp white (`#FFFFFF`) cards, floating panels, and modals layered over a clean warm-neutral off-white workspace canvas (`#FAFAFA`).\\n    - **30% Structural Surfaces**: Deep charcoal (`#111827`) for primary headers, destination titles, and prices; neutral slate (`#4B5563`) for secondary metadata; and crisp hairline borders (`border-neutral-200/80`).\\n    - **10% Accent Budget**: Vibrant Sunset Orange (`#FF812E`, hover `#E56B1A`) reserved strictly for primary CTAs, active route highlights, numbered map pins, and primary geodesic flight/transit arcs, paired with soft orange tint (`#FFF4ED`) and warm border (`#FFD6BA`) for active card states.\\n    - **Semantic Status**: Green (`#16A34A`) for savings/applied vouchers, Amber (`#D97706`) for long layovers, Crimson (`#DC2626`) for invalid vouchers or warnings\342\200\224always paired with explicit text labels.\\n  - *Typography & Hierarchy*:\\n    - Display & Headings: `Plus Jakarta Sans` (SemiBold/Bold) with `text-wrap: balance` on titles.\\n    - Body & Controls: `DM Sans` (Regular/Medium) at 13px\342\200\22315px for crisp legibility.\\n    - Numeric Telemetry: `JetBrains Mono` with `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` for fares, Smart Scores, durations, coordinates, and promo codes.\\n  - *Component Styling & Layout*:\\n    - **Top Bar Contract**: Clean single-row header with three zones (`Astris Travel` wordmark \342\200\224 concise workspace section links \342\200\224 single `#FF812E` `Optimize Route` primary CTA).\\n    - **Split-Screen Master Layout**: Full-viewport `1440px` desktop split (`46%` scrollable itinerary & transit inspector on the left over `#FAFAFA`, `54%` sticky interactive MapLibre canvas on the right, responsive stacked toggle on mobile).\\n    - **Card & Metadata Restraint**: Single-elevation pure white `rounded-2xl` cards (`bg-white border border-neutral-200/80 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md`), active selection cards using `#FFF4ED` tint with `#FFD6BA` border, clean unboxed metadata joined by typographic separators (`\302\267`, `/`), and zero nested card-in-card clutter or thick left accent borders.\\n    - **Map & Glassmorphic Controls**: Numbered destination pins (`1`, `2`, `3`, `4`...) and primary active flight/transit arcs rendered in `#FF812E` with soft white halos/outlines (`#FFFFFF`) on pins so they pop clearly against map tiles; floating segmented transport filter bar (`All`, `Flight`, `Train`, `Bus`) over the map styled with `bg-white/85 backdrop-blur-md border border-white/40 shadow-lg rounded-full`.\", \"StartLine\":36, \"TargetContent\":\"- **Visual Identity & Theme**:\\n  - *Aesthetic Direction*: Modern, airy travel-tech workspace blending editorial clarity with high-precision SaaS utility (Airbnb warmth meets Wanderlog spatial structure).\\n  - *Color Palette & Mood*:\\n    - **60% Dominant Neutral Canvas**: Crisp white (`#FFFFFF`) panels and soft slate-tinted workspace canvas (`bg-slate-50`).\\n    - **30% Structural Surfaces**: Deep midnight slate typography (`text-slate-900` primary, `text-slate-600` secondary, `text-slate-500` metadata) and hairline borders (`border-slate-200/80`).\\n    - **10% Accent Budget**: Electric indigo (`bg-indigo-600 hover:bg-indigo-700 text-white`, `text-indigo-600`) reserved strictly for primary CTAs, active route highlights, numbered map pins, and selected transit states.\\n    - **Semantic Status**: Green (`#16A34A`) for savings/applied vouchers, Amber (`#D97706`) for long layovers, Crimson (`#DC2626`) for invalid vouchers or warnings\342\200\224always paired with explicit text labels.\\n  - *Typography & Hierarchy*:\\n    - Display & Headings: `Plus Jakarta Sans` (SemiBold/Bold) with `text-wrap: balance` on titles.\\n    - Body & Controls: `DM Sans` (Regular/Medium) at 13px\342\200\22315px for crisp legibility.\\n    - Numeric Telemetry: `JetBrains Mono` with `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` for fares, Smart Scores, durations, coordinates, and promo codes.\\n  - *Component Styling & Layout*:\\n    - **Top Bar Contract**: Clean single-row header with three zones (`Astris Travel` wordmark \342\200\224 concise workspace section links \342\200\224 single `Optimize Route` primary CTA).\\n    - **Split-Screen Master Layout**: Full-viewport `1440px` desktop split (`46%` scrollable itinerary & transit inspector on the left, `54%` sticky interactive MapLibre canvas on the right, responsive stacked toggle on mobile).\\n    - **Card & Metadata Restraint**: Single-elevation `rounded-2xl` cards (`border border-slate-200/80 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md`), clean unboxed metadata joined by typographic separators (`\302\267`, `/`), and zero nested card-in-card clutter or thick left accent borders.\\n    - **Glassmorphic Map Controls**: Floating segmented transport filter bar (`All`, `Flight`, `Train`, `Bus`) and leg summary overlay positioned over the map using `bg-white/80 backdrop-blur-md border border-white/20 shadow-lg rounded-full`.\", \"TargetFile\":\"/.aistudio/artifacts/brain/fb7c045e-904d-498c-ad70-52c85fbc80f0/implementation_plan.md\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating plan design system to Sunset Orange\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update plan color palette\"}"
