  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Synthesizing Phase 1**\n\nOkay, I\'m making good progress! The implementation plan is approved, and the `metadata.json` file now correctly includes `\"name\": \"Astris Travel\"`. I\'m starting to focus on synthesizing all three sources, beginning with Phase 1 Clarifications to ensure complete integration of all the data.\n\n\n**Defining Core Technologies**\n\nI\'ve decided on the core technologies: a live React + Vite + Express app running on port 3000, and FastAPI/Pydantic v2 reference models for the backend. I\'m moving forward with a token-free MapLibre GL implementation, using `maplibre-gl`, `react-map-gl`, and `@turf/great-circle`. My focus now is on creating a full interactive split-screen workspace using a mock dataset, starting with mock dataset API endpoints in Express.\n\n\n**Refining the UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into UI refinements! I\'m focusing on the visual hierarchy, incorporating numbered pins and curved flight arcs on the map using MapLibre GL. I\'m building out the glassmorphism transport filter bar and finalizing the typography, specifying fonts and their use cases. Additionally, the top bar contract for the header is well-defined, and I\'m ensuring single-elevation cards create a clean visual flow.\n\n\n**Structuring the Components**\n\nI\'m now focused on component organization! I\'ve chosen `/shared` for TypeScript models and mock data, including the Smart Score engine, and `/backend` for FastAPI models and optimization logic. I\'m prioritizing clean separation of concerns and maintainability, ensuring that the backend will include a `/models` directory. I\'m planning for a clean implementation in the `/backend` using a realistic four-stop trip JSON mock dataset with extra hubs.\n\n\n**Defining the API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now nailing down the API endpoints! I have a clear vision for the `/server.ts` Express server, including essential endpoints such as `/api/trips/default`, `/api/destinations`, `/api/legs/options`, `/api/optimize-route`, `/api/vouchers`, and `/api/vouchers/validate`. I\'m committed to a modular React component structure with specific components, and planning a single batched `install_applet_package` call for needed packages, including `@dnd-kit/core`, `maplibre-gl`, and several other critical libraries. I\'m also ensuring React 19 compatibility.\n\n\n"
