  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Updating Configuration Details**\n\nI\'m currently updating the `package.json` file. I\'ve configured the \"dev\" and \"start\" scripts for the project. Simultaneously, I\'m working to create `/shared/types.ts` to implement clean TypeScript contracts for the `Trip` type. This will involve defining clear, concise type definitions.\n\n\n**Defining Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining data structures. I\'ve got `TripStop`, `TripLeg`, `TransitOption`, `SmartScoreBreakdown`, `Voucher`, `RouteOptimizationResult`, `VttsTier`, `TransitMode`, and `DestinationHub` laid out. I\'m building a pure TypeScript implementation of the tiered VTTS Smart Score engine in `/shared/smartScore.ts`. This will include Haversine distance, voucher evaluation, and dynamic leg transit generation, which will allow for stop reordering. I\'m also creating a mock dataset at `/shared/mockDataset.ts`. This mock dataset will model a 4-stop trip with multimodal options.\n\n\n**Calculating Smart Score Logic**\n\nI\'m now calculating the smart score logic. I\'ve defined different explorer options, including balanced, express, and custom. The formula weighs factors like mode multiplier, layover, and in-vehicle time to determine the smart score. I\'m focusing on making the trade-offs realistic and evident in the data. For instance, the Eurostar direct example from London to Paris would be evaluated as `$118 + (2.3 * 15 * 1) + (0 * 15 * 0)`.\n\n\n**Evaluating Travel Options**\n\nI\'m now evaluating various travel options with smart score calculations. For the London to Paris route, I\'ve calculated the smart scores for Eurostar, British Airways, and BlaBlaCar/FlixBus. I\'m focusing on the impact of factors like base price, in-vehicle time, and layover time, at different hourly rate assumptions. For overnight coach examples, I\'m specifically weighing the \"isOvernightSleeper\" factor and updating the weights to reflect realistic trade-offs between cost and time-saving. I\'m trying to ensure that daytime train options, like the Eurostar, win at the express `$35/hr` option.\n\n\n**Calculating New Scores**\n\nI\'m now calculating more smart scores for multi-leg flights and multimodal options. For Istanbul to London, I\'ve evaluated Turkish Airlines direct, Pegasus with a stop in Ankara, Aegean via Athens, and a Balkan train/Eurostar combination. I\'ve also run Kuala Lumpur to Istanbul examples with direct and one-stop flights, assessing the impact of layover times and overnight considerations. I\'m noting the results from different hourly rate assumptions.\n\n\n"
