  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Incorporate New Schema**\n\nOkay, I\'ve taken note of the user\'s explicit request to integrate the PostgreSQL database schema provided. I\'m actively working to understand the schema\'s structure and how it fits within the overall architecture. My immediate goal is to figure out the best way to incorporate the schema into the backend files, making the database a central component.\n\n\n**Refine Integration Strategy**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a clean integration of the PostgreSQL schema. My plan is to keep the user\'s `SCHEMA.sql` file verbatim in `/backend/SCHEMA.sql`, adding any necessary changes as non-breaking `ALTER` statements or comments. I\'m carefully reviewing `/backend/models.py` and `/shared/types.ts` to align them with the schema, specifically checking the mapping of columns in `users`, `trips`, `trip_legs`, `transit_options`, and `vouchers`. The goal is to prepare for future persistence integration without immediate Cloud SQL provisioning.\n\n\n**Detail Schema Amendments**\n\nI\'ve got the schema amendments clearly in sight now. I need to update the `models.py` and `types.ts` files to reflect the new additions: `UserProfile`, `\'ferry\'` to the `TransitMode` enum, and so on. Also, the plan includes optional fields like `booking_url` and `platform_source`, plus I need to get the database schema ready with SQLAlchemy/asyncpg/psycopg, and add a schema contract reference, so I am planning out the code for this in `database.py`. The `implementation_plan.md` section needs an update as well.\n\n\n**Verify Type Usage**\n\nI\'m now focused on verifying the usage of the `TransitMode` enum across the codebase, particularly concerning the proposed addition of `\'ferry\'`. I\'m checking `/src/components/WorldMapCanvas.tsx` to ensure that adding this new mode doesn\'t break any existing logic, specifically the exhaustive switch statement, by manually inspecting line 153. I\'m also planning a more comprehensive `grep` search for `TransitMode` to identify all relevant code sections for review. My aim is to maintain type safety and prevent runtime errors.\n\n\n**Detail Implementation Steps**\n\nI\'m now outlining the implementation steps in detail. I\'ll create `/backend/SCHEMA.sql` directly from the user\'s PostgreSQL schema and build a connection/repository stub, `/backend/database.py`, for Supabase/PostgreSQL. I need to update `/backend/models.py` and `/shared/types.ts` to include `UserProfile`, `\'ferry\'` mode, plus optional fields, and align everything with `SCHEMA.sql`. Also, I\'m planning to use `<Ship />` icon in `ModeIcon` for ferry to manage ferry display correctly. Finally, I will ensure adding the ferry option to `counts` in `WorldMapCanvas.tsx` to handle ferry data correctly, and prevent TypeScript errors.\n\n\n"
