          end_line: 134
          unified_diff {
            lines {
              text: "# Astris Travel \342\200\224 Implementation Plan"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "Astris Travel is a split-screen multi-destination travel planning and route optimization workspace that pairs an interactive drag-and-drop itinerary timeline with a synchronized geodesic world map, multi-modal transit comparison, Smart Score ranking, two-stage route optimization, and automatic voucher matching."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "---"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "### User Review & Critical Decisions"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "> [!IMPORTANT]"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "> All core architectural choices below incorporate your Phase 1 answers and govern how the live preview, mapping engine, and shared data contracts are structured."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Confirmed Decision 1 \342\200\224 Hybrid Live Runtime + FastAPI Schemas**: Build a live, immediately previewable React + Vite + Express TypeScript application on port 3000 while also delivering the shared TypeScript contracts and Python FastAPI + Pydantic v2 models (`Trip`, `TripLeg`, `TransitOption`, `Voucher`) alongside the structured JSON mock dataset."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Confirmed Decision 2 \342\200\224 Token-Free MapLibre GL**: Use `react-map-gl` (MapLibre entrypoint) paired with `maplibre-gl` and `@turf/great-circle` over a clean, token-free Carto Positron vector/raster basemap so numbered destination pins and curved geodesic flight arcs render reliably with zero API key friction."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Confirmed Decision 3 \342\200\224 Full Interactive Workspace**: Ship the complete split-screen workspace upfront, including drag-and-drop stop reordering, adding/removing destinations, live Smart Score recalculation, two-stage route optimization, and interactive voucher application."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Confirmed Decision 4 \342\200\224 Mock Dataset + Express API Endpoints First**: Back the interactive client with Express `/api/*` endpoints serving and evaluating the realistic 4-stop `Kuala Lumpur \342\206\222 Istanbul \342\206\222 London \342\206\222 Paris` dataset (plus expandable global hubs), keeping persistence lightweight before connecting live transit feeds or PostgreSQL."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "---"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "### 1. Overview & Core Concept"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **What It Does**: Users build and refine multi-city international itineraries in a synchronized split-screen workspace. Reordering or adding stops on the left timeline immediately updates numbered pins and great-circle flight arcs on the right map, queries multi-modal door-to-door transit options (flights, high-speed rail, and intercity coaches), ranks them via the Smart Score formula, applies eligible promo vouchers, and runs a two-stage geographical + transit optimizer to suggest better stop sequences."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Target Audience / Persona**: Global travelers, digital nomads, and multi-leg trip planners balancing ticket cost against travel and layover hours across air and ground transport."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Key Value**: Eliminates multi-tab spreadsheet planning by quantifying the true comfort-weighted, time-adjusted cost of every leg (`discountedPrice + (inVehicleHours \303\227 baseRate \303\227 modeMultiplier) + (layoverHours \303\227 baseRate \303\227 layoverMultiplier)`) and immediately visualizing route geometry and savings on one canvas."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "---"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "### 2. User Experience & Visual Design"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Key User Flows**:"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "  1. **Initial Workspace Load**: Opens directly into the pre-loaded 4-stop trip (`1. Kuala Lumpur \342\206\222 2. Istanbul \342\206\222 3. London \342\206\222 4. Paris`), displaying total trip cost, total travel hours, the active **Balanced Explorer (`$15/hr`)** VTTS tier, and numbered geodesic arcs across Asia and Europe."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "  2. **Timeline & Map Synchronization**: Users drag stops by their grip handle to reorder the sequence, hover over any stop or leg to highlight its corresponding pin and curved arc on the map, click a leg to inspect door-to-door flight/train/bus alternatives, or add/remove stops from a searchable destination picker."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "  3. **Tiered VTTS Smart Score & Multi-Modal Filtering**: Switching between the 3-tier Value of Travel Time Savings (VTTS) preset toggle (**Budget Backpacker** `$5/hr`, **Balanced Explorer** `$15/hr` default, **Time-Rich / Express** `$35/hr`), optionally expanding the advanced fine-tuning slider, or toggling the floating glassmorphic transport filter bar (`All`, `Flight`, `Train`, `Bus`) over the map dynamically recalculates pain-weighted Smart Scores and re-ranks transit cards in real time."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "  4. **Two-Stage Route Optimizer**: Clicking **Optimize Route** in the top bar runs Stage 1 (local geographical permutation scoring via Haversine/great-circle distance) and Stage 2 (Express API transit evaluation of top paths), presenting a comparison drawer with net distance, hours, and cost deltas that can be applied in one click."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "  5. **Voucher & Promo Matching**: Users enter a promo code or toggle matched eligible vouchers on a selected transit option; the engine validates corridor, mode, carrier, and minimum spend rules, updating the net fare and Smart Score inline."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Visual Identity & Theme**:"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Aesthetic Direction*: Modern, airy travel-tech workspace blending editorial clarity with high-precision SaaS utility (Airbnb warmth meets Wanderlog spatial structure)."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Color Palette & Mood*:"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    - **60% Dominant Neutral Canvas**: Pure crisp white (`#FFFFFF`) cards, floating panels, and modals layered over a clean warm-neutral off-white workspace canvas (`#FAFAFA`)."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    - **30% Structural Surfaces**: Deep charcoal (`#111827`) for primary headers, destination titles, and prices; neutral slate (`#4B5563`) for secondary metadata; and crisp hairline borders (`border-neutral-200/80`)."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    - **10% Accent Budget**: Vibrant Sunset Orange (`#FF812E`, hover `#E56B1A`) reserved strictly for primary CTAs, active route highlights, numbered map pins, and primary geodesic flight/transit arcs, paired with soft orange tint (`#FFF4ED`) and warm border (`#FFD6BA`) for active card states."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    - **Semantic Status**: Green (`#16A34A`) for savings/applied vouchers, Amber (`#D97706`) for long layovers, Crimson (`#DC2626`) for invalid vouchers or warnings\342\200\224always paired with explicit text labels."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Typography & Hierarchy*:"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    - Display & Headings: `Plus Jakarta Sans` (SemiBold/Bold) with `text-wrap: balance` on titles."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    - Body & Controls: `DM Sans` (Regular/Medium) at 13px\342\200\22315px for crisp legibility."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    - Numeric Telemetry: `JetBrains Mono` with `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` for fares, Smart Scores, durations, coordinates, and promo codes."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Component Styling & Layout*:"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    - **Top Bar Contract**: Clean single-row header with three zones (`Astris Travel` wordmark \342\200\224 concise workspace section links \342\200\224 single `#FF812E` `Optimize Route` primary CTA)."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    - **Split-Screen Master Layout**: Full-viewport `1440px` desktop split (`46%` scrollable itinerary & transit inspector on the left over `#FAFAFA`, `54%` sticky interactive MapLibre canvas on the right, responsive stacked toggle on mobile)."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    - **Card & Metadata Restraint**: Single-elevation pure white `rounded-2xl` cards (`bg-white border border-neutral-200/80 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md`), active selection cards using `#FFF4ED` tint with `#FFD6BA` border, clean unboxed metadata joined by typographic separators (`\302\267`, `/`), and zero nested card-in-card clutter or thick left accent borders."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "    - **Map & Glassmorphic Controls**: Numbered destination pins (`1`, `2`, `3`, `4`...) and primary active flight/transit arcs rendered in `#FF812E` with soft white halos/outlines (`#FFFFFF`) on pins so they pop clearly against map tiles; floating segmented transport filter bar (`All`, `Flight`, `Train`, `Bus`) over the map styled with `bg-white/85 backdrop-blur-md border border-white/40 shadow-lg rounded-full`."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Interactive Feedback & Motion**:"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - Smooth 150\342\200\223200ms transitions (`cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)`) using `transform` and `opacity` during drag sorting, leg expansion, and map camera `flyTo` transitions."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - Complete empty state (when fewer than 2 stops remain), loading skeleton state during route optimization, and non-blocking inline error/validation feedback for promo codes."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "---"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "### 3. Key Product Decisions & Trade-Offs"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Decision 1 \342\200\224 Live Express + React Architecture Alongside FastAPI/Pydantic Blueprint**:"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Chosen Approach*: Serve the interactive React frontend and REST endpoints from a unified Express + Vite Node server on port 3000, while placing clean, production-ready Python FastAPI + Pydantic v2 model definitions and router specs in a dedicated backend reference module."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Why*: Ensures the application launches and runs live immediately in the preview environment without requiring a separate Python ASGI runtime, while honoring the exact Pydantic v2 data contracts needed for future Python microservice deployment."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Alternatives Considered*: A static Next.js + FastAPI folder scaffold was passed over because it would leave the port-3000 preview non-functional."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Decision 2 \342\200\224 MapLibre GL (`react-map-gl/maplibre`) + `@turf/great-circle`**:"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Chosen Approach*: Render the interactive world map with MapLibre GL and free Carto Positron vector/raster styles, drawing smooth spherical great-circle GeoJSON lines and custom HTML numbered markers."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Why*: Delivers smooth pan/zoom, `flyTo` synchronization, and crisp curved arcs immediately with zero access-token failures."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Alternatives Considered*: Raw Mapbox GL requires a private token that breaks in tokenless previews; static SVG maps lack real zoom/pan exploration."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Decision 3 \342\200\224 Tiered VTTS Smart Score Engine & Two-Stage Optimizer**:"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Chosen Approach*: Compute interactive Smart Score updates instantaneously on the client when toggling the 3-tier VTTS preset (`$5/hr`, `$15/hr`, `$35/hr`) or scrubbing the optional advanced slider, using phase-weighted pain multipliers (`0.4\303\227` overnight sleeper, `1.0\303\227` standard in-vehicle or short transfer `<2h`, `1.5\303\227` normal layover `2\342\200\2235h`, `2.5\303\227` long layover `6+h`), while routing Two-Stage Route Optimization and Voucher Validation through dedicated Express `/api/*` endpoints."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Why*: Realistic VTTS presets prevent unrealistic distortions on long-haul flights while rewarding sleeper trains and penalizing grueling 6+ hour airport layovers; client-side recalculation keeps preset/slider transitions instantaneous."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              text: "---"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
            }
