  planner_response {
    response: "The PostgreSQL database schema (`SCHEMA.sql`) has been incorporated into the backend and shared data contracts so the application is ready for database persistence:\n\n- **PostgreSQL DDL (`SCHEMA.sql`):** Added the complete schema covering `users`, `trips`, `trip_legs`, `transit_options`, and `vouchers`, including `uuid-ossp`, foreign key constraints (`fk_selected_option`, `fk_applied_voucher`), and performance indexes (`idx_trip_legs_trip_order`, `idx_transit_options_leg_score`, `idx_vouchers_active_provider`).\n- **Backend Persistence Helper:** Added `database.py` with `DATABASE_URL` environment lookup, DDL loader, and parameterized SQL query templates matching the five tables.\n- **Aligned Pydantic v2 & TypeScript Contracts:** Updated `UserProfile`, `Trip`, `TripLeg`, `TransitOption`, and `Voucher` across both Python and TypeScript to include `ferry` mode support, `booking_url`, `platform_source`, `valid_from`, `is_active`, `is_route_optimized`, and `start_date`/`end_date`, and updated the implementation plan\'s data model reference.\n- **Verification:** Confirmed zero TypeScript errors (`tsc --noEmit`) and a clean Vite production build."
