  user_input {
    user_response: "Please perform the following UI cleanup, map tile fix, and Rome2Rio-style multi-modal map upgrade across our React components and MapLibre workspace:\n\n### 1. UI Text Audit & Cleanup\n- Audit all dashboard, timeline, and card components and remove all unnecessary descriptive text, tutorial blurbs, helper paragraphs, and instructional sentences (e.g., remove \"Drag stops by the grip handle...\", VTTS explanations, etc.).\n- Keep only essential labels, telemetry numbers, status badges, and interactive controls for a clean, high-density SaaS layout.\n\n### 2. Fix Map Basemap (Remove Watermarks)\n- Replace the broken Carto basemap style URL (which currently renders \"API KEY REQUIRED\" watermarks) with a clean, token-free MapLibre basemap style (such as OpenFreeMap `https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/positron` or clean OSM raster tiles) so the world map renders crisply with zero watermarks.\n\n### 3. Rome2Rio-Style Multi-Modal Lines, Sub-Segments & Floating Callouts\nUpgrade `MapWorkspace` so every trip leg renders detailed, mode-distinct routing between nodes:\n- **Multi-Segment Door-to-Door Paths:** Support chaining sub-segments per leg (e.g., local airport rail transfer \342\206\222 main flight \342\206\222 arrival transit) with small white-bordered junction nodes (`8px` circles with white stroke) at transfer points.\n- **Mode-Specific Line Colors & Geometry:**\n  - **Flights:** Smooth, sweeping spherical great-circle arcs (`@turf/great-circle`) rendered in **Sunset Orange (`#FF812E`)**, `3px` width, with a directional airplane marker/icon along the arc.\n  - **Trains:** Road/rail-following multi-point GeoJSON polylines rendered in **Emerald/Teal (`#0D9488`)** with intermediate station dots along the path.\n  - **Buses & Local Transfers:** Multi-point ground polylines rendered in **Royal Purple (`#7C3AED`)** with intermediate stop dots.\n- **Floating White Callout Pills on Map:** Render compact, glassmorphic/white floating callout cards (`bg-white/95 backdrop-blur-sm shadow-md rounded-xl px-2.5 py-1.5 border border-slate-200/80`) anchored near key hubs/legs displaying:\n  - Step/Leg number, color-coded transport icon (plane/train/bus), hub/city name, and duration (e.g., `1 \360\237\232\206 KLIA Ekspres \302\267 32m` or `2 \342\234\210\357\270\217 Istanbul (IST) \302\267 11h 12m`)."
    items {
      text: "Please perform the following UI cleanup, map tile fix, and Rome2Rio-style multi-modal map upgrade across our React components and MapLibre workspace:\n\n### 1. UI Text Audit & Cleanup\n- Audit all dashboard, timeline, and card components and remove all unnecessary descriptive text, tutorial blurbs, helper paragraphs, and instructional sentences (e.g., remove \"Drag stops by the grip handle...\", VTTS explanations, etc.).\n- Keep only essential labels, telemetry numbers, status badges, and interactive controls for a clean, high-density SaaS layout.\n\n### 2. Fix Map Basemap (Remove Watermarks)\n- Replace the broken Carto basemap style URL (which currently renders \"API KEY REQUIRED\" watermarks) with a clean, token-free MapLibre basemap style (such as OpenFreeMap `https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/positron` or clean OSM raster tiles) so the world map renders crisply with zero watermarks.\n\n### 3. Rome2Rio-Style Multi-Modal Lines, Sub-Segments & Floating Callouts\nUpgrade `MapWorkspace` so every trip leg renders detailed, mode-distinct routing between nodes:\n- **Multi-Segment Door-to-Door Paths:** Support chaining sub-segments per leg (e.g., local airport rail transfer \342\206\222 main flight \342\206\222 arrival transit) with small white-bordered junction nodes (`8px` circles with white stroke) at transfer points.\n- **Mode-Specific Line Colors & Geometry:**\n  - **Flights:** Smooth, sweeping spherical great-circle arcs (`@turf/great-circle`) rendered in **Sunset Orange (`#FF812E`)**, `3px` width, with a directional airplane marker/icon along the arc.\n  - **Trains:** Road/rail-following multi-point GeoJSON polylines rendered in **Emerald/Teal (`#0D9488`)** with intermediate station dots along the path.\n  - **Buses & Local Transfers:** Multi-point ground polylines rendered in **Royal Purple (`#7C3AED`)** with intermediate stop dots.\n- **Floating White Callout Pills on Map:** Render compact, glassmorphic/white floating callout cards (`bg-white/95 backdrop-blur-sm shadow-md rounded-xl px-2.5 py-1.5 border border-slate-200/80`) anchored near key hubs/legs displaying:\n  - Step/Leg number, color-coded transport icon (plane/train/bus), hub/city name, and duration (e.g., `1 \360\237\232\206 KLIA Ekspres \302\267 32m` or `2 \342\234\210\357\270\217 Istanbul (IST) \302\267 11h 12m`)."
    }
  }
}
