  planner_response {
    response: "The UI cleanup, watermark-free map basemap switch, and Rome2Rio-style multi-modal routing visualization are complete:\n\n### 1. High-Density UI Text Audit & Cleanup\n- Removed explanatory paragraphs, drag-and-drop tutorial blurbs, VTTS descriptions, and verbose transit prose across the dashboard, timeline cards, VTTS controls, add-stop modal, route optimizer modal, and voucher drawer.\n- Retained essential labels, tabular telemetry figures, Smart Score breakdowns, and compact sub-segment step chains (e.g., `KLIA Ekspres (28m) \342\206\222 TK 61 (672m) \342\206\222 M11 Metro (38m)`).\n\n### 2. Token-Free, Watermark-Free Map Basemap\n- Switched the MapLibre basemap style to OpenFreeMap Positron (`https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/positron`) with an OpenStreetMap raster tile fallback, eliminating Carto `\"API KEY REQUIRED\"` watermarks.\n\n### 3. Rome2Rio-Style Multi-Modal Map Routing & Callouts\n- **Multi-Segment Door-to-Door Paths:** Added `TransitSegment` chains across curated and synthesized corridors (linking city-center rail/coach transfers, main flights/trains, and arrival transit) with white-bordered junction nodes at transfer points.\n- **Mode-Specific Colors & Geometry:**\n  - **Flights (`#FF812E`):** Sweeping `@turf/great-circle` arcs (`3px` base, `4.2px` highlighted) with bearing-rotated airplane icons at arc midpoints.\n  - **Trains (`#0D9488`):** Multi-point rail GeoJSON polylines with intermediate station dots.\n  - **Buses (`#7C3AED`):** Multi-point ground coach polylines with intermediate stop dots.\n- **Floating Map Callout Pills:** Anchored compact white glassmorphic callout pills (`bg-white/95 backdrop-blur-sm`) near key legs and highlighted transfer segments showing leg number, mode icon, corridor/service label, and duration.\n\n### Verification\n- Verified `tsc --noEmit`, `vite build`, dev server restart on port 3000, and live `/api/trips/default` responses with multi-modal `segments`."
    modified_response: "The UI cleanup, watermark-free map basemap switch, and Rome2Rio-style multi-modal routing visualization are complete:\n\n### 1. High-Density UI Text Audit & Cleanup\n- Removed explanatory paragraphs, drag-and-drop tutorial blurbs, VTTS descriptions, and verbose transit prose across the dashboard, timeline cards, VTTS controls, add-stop modal, route optimizer modal, and voucher drawer.\n- Retained essential labels, tabular telemetry figures, Smart Score breakdowns, and compact sub-segment step chains (e.g., `KLIA Ekspres (28m) \342\206\222 TK 61 (672m) \342\206\222 M11 Metro (38m)`).\n\n### 2. Token-Free, Watermark-Free Map Basemap\n- Switched the MapLibre basemap style to OpenFreeMap Positron (`https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/positron`) with an OpenStreetMap raster tile fallback, eliminating Carto `\"API KEY REQUIRED\"` watermarks.\n\n### 3. Rome2Rio-Style Multi-Modal Map Routing & Callouts\n- **Multi-Segment Door-to-Door Paths:** Added `TransitSegment` chains across curated and synthesized corridors (linking city-center rail/coach transfers, main flights/trains, and arrival transit) with white-bordered junction nodes at transfer points.\n- **Mode-Specific Colors & Geometry:**\n  - **Flights (`#FF812E`):** Sweeping `@turf/great-circle` arcs (`3px` base, `4.2px` highlighted) with bearing-rotated airplane icons at arc midpoints.\n  - **Trains (`#0D9488`):** Multi-point rail GeoJSON polylines with intermediate station dots.\n  - **Buses (`#7C3AED`):** Multi-point ground coach polylines with intermediate stop dots.\n- **Floating Map Callout Pills:** Anchored compact white glassmorphic callout pills (`bg-white/95 backdrop-blur-sm`) near key legs and highlighted transfer segments showing leg number, mode icon, corridor/service label, and duration.\n\n### Verification\n- Verified `tsc --noEmit`, `vite build`, dev server restart on port 3000, and live `/api/trips/default` responses with multi-modal `segments`."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    thinking_signature: "\022\353\001\n\350\001\001i\024}\023\366.\326\327@\357\366/\273\277 <\235\024\\P\343V\226<\360\r\027\252H^\212\320b\325Ac\201I\234\253}\t\207\317\005\3518%\334`\fs\364>\350\f\221\006\003\316\227\020\202$\221\330\325\b&6\246\271\215\364/\377\177a{8\"\2405|1\"\265\005\017\246\225\322\347S\351\354\310\216\212v\371?A\303\026\202>/&\355K\251W\027\024R|\250/}\227s+\3120w\345(\247\341\313\200L&\265%a\317\232J\206\262vy\350\251\255Iz\214\022)\206qf\321{\033\017i1W\325\273\031\356\213\003+5\243qL\246O\327\316\004z\025\276\220-YzsI\232\223q\216$r\230\202pKT\240\002\365\024\374\252g\262\313i\apV\255M\226\365:\327\222)\252\240\220\0315\017b8f\336~p"
