    model_api_content_id: "MMT3avqkM-yI6dkPlu-B2Ac"
  }
  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Visual Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the visual requirements for the multi-destination date picker. Specifically, I\'m focusing on its aesthetic integration within the Astris Light Theme. This includes ensuring proper contrast and harmonious color usage, considering the `#FFFFFF` card background over the `#FAFAFA` canvas, `#111827` text, and `#FF812E` Sunset Orange accent. My goal is a visually seamless and accessible component.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the multi-destination date picker into the Astris Light Theme, with an emphasis on crisp visuals. I\'ve confirmed a white floating popover with a subtle border and shadow, utilizing \"Plus Jakarta Sans\" for the header and \"JetBrains Mono\" for the numbers. I\'m focusing on triggering the component from date badges on stop cards and a trip-level date range button. I\'m assigning distinct badge colors to each stop, starting with Sunset Orange for the active selection, and other distinct color keys.\n\n\n**Visualizing Night Bookings**\n\nI\'m now determining how to represent booked nights across calendar dates. I\'m assigning distinct colors to each stop: Sunset Orange for the selected stop, and Teal, Purple, Amber, etc. for the remaining stops. I\'m focusing on rendering each city\'s booked nights from arrival to departure. My current thought is to highlight the range from arrival to departure, exclusive of the departure date to cleanly display stays.\n\n\n**Clarifying Calendar Visualization**\n\nMy focus is clarifying calendar visualizations. I plan to represent booked nights cleanly as continuous, rounded pill ranges, using arrival and departure dates to define each stay. I\'m aiming for no messy overlaps on handoff days by rendering `[arrivalDate, departureDate)`. I\'ll allow users to click arrival and departure dates to calculate `stayNights`. I\'ll also implement a hover preview, showing the live range and night count, as well as a color-dot legend mapping cities to colors.\n\n\n**Synchronizing Date Selections**\n\nI\'m now implementing two-way state synchronization. Selecting dates in the calendar will update the `arrivalDate`, `departureDate`, and `stayNights` for the active stop. I\'m focusing on the date cascade to handle subsequent stop dates automatically, preserving night counts and transit gaps. I\'m leveraging pure UTC date utilities (`parseIsoDate`, `addDaysIso`, `diffDaysIso`) to avoid timezone issues. When a stop\'s dates change, I\'ll update that stop and then cascade the dates. I also plan to make clicking a city in the color legend switch which stop is currently active.\n\n\n**Updating Date Logic**\n\nI\'m refining the date logic, starting with a stop\'s night counter update, which directly affects its departure date, using `departureDate = addDaysIso(arrivalDate, newNights)`. My focus is on cascading updates to subsequent stops, preserving the original transit gaps. I\'m exploring how to shift all later stops by `deltaDays` to keep the overnight flight gaps intact. I\'m also ensuring that the stop\'s night counter update updates the entire calendar timeline.\n\n\n**Sequencing Stop Dates**\n\nI\'m now focusing on date reordering through dragging. I\'ve realized that recalculating sequential dates from the trip\'s start date preserves `stayNights` and maintains contiguous dates. Moving a stop updates arrival and departure dates, and the others cascade with a 1-day buffer when leg duration exceeds 10 hours. Adding/removing stops also keeps sequential dates clean and synchronized. I\'m building a shared date utility for ISO date arithmetic.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_6058876144491997498"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import type { TripLeg, TripStop } from \'./types.ts\';\\n\\nexport const STOP_BADGE_PALETTE = [\\n  \'#FF812E\', // Selected / Primary Sunset Orange\\n  \'#0D9488\', // Teal\\n  \'#7C3AED\', // Purple\\n  \'#D97706\', // Amber\\n  \'#0284C7\', // Sky\\n  \'#E11D48\', // Rose\\n];\\n\\nexport function parseIsoUtc(isoDate: string): Date {\\n  const [y, m, d] = isoDate.split(\'-\').map(Number);\\n  return new Date(Date.UTC(y, (m || 1) - 1, d || 1));\\n}\\n\\nexport function formatIsoUtc(date: Date): string {\\n  const y = date.getUTCFullYear();\\n  const m = String(date.getUTCMonth() + 1).padStart(2, \'0\');\\n  const d = String(date.getUTCDate()).padStart(2, \'0\');\\n  return `${y}-${m}-${d}`;\\n}\\n\\nexport function addDaysIso(isoDate: string, days: number): string {\\n  const dt = parseIsoUtc(isoDate);\\n  dt.setUTCDate(dt.getUTCDate() + days);\\n  return formatIsoUtc(dt);\\n}\\n\\nexport function diffDaysIso(startIso: string, endIso: string): number {\\n  const msPerDay = 86_400_000;\\n  return Math.round(\\n    (parseIsoUtc(endIso).getTime() - parseIsoUtc(startIso).getTime()) / msPerDay\\n  );\\n}\\n\\nexport function formatShortDate(isoDate: string): string {\\n  const dt = parseIsoUtc(isoDate);\\n  return dt.toLocaleDateString(\'en-US\', {\\n    month: \'short\',\\n    day: \'numeric\',\\n    timeZone: \'UTC\',\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nexport function formatTripDateSpan(stops: TripStop[]): string {\\n  if (stops.length === 0) return \'Select dates\';\\n  const first = stops[0].arrivalDate;\\n  const last = stops[stops.length - 1].departureDate;\\n  const firstYear = parseIsoUtc(first).getUTCFullYear();\\n  const lastYear = parseIsoUtc(last).getUTCFullYear();\\n  if (firstYear === lastYear) {\\n    return `${formatShortDate(first)} \342\200\223 ${formatShortDate(last)}, ${lastYear}`;\\n  }\\n  return `${formatShortDate(first)} ${firstYear} \342\200\223 ${formatShortDate(last)} ${lastYear}`;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Updates a single stop\'s arrival/departure/nights and shifts all subsequent stops\\n * by the departure date delta so transit gaps are preserved and dates never collide.\\n */\\nexport function updateStopDatesAndCascade(\\n  stops: TripStop[],\\n  targetStopId: string,\\n  newArrivalDate: string,\\n  newDepartureDate: string\\n): TripStop[] {\\n  const targetIdx = stops.findIndex((s) => s.id === targetStopId);\\n  if (targetIdx === -1) return stops;\\n\\n  const oldStop = stops[targetIdx];\\n  const stayNights = Math.max(1, diffDaysIso(newArrivalDate, newDepartureDate));\\n  const resolvedDeparture = addDaysIso(newArrivalDate, stayNights);\\n  const departureDelta = diffDaysIso(oldStop.departureDate, resolvedDeparture);\\n\\n  return stops.map((stop, idx) => {\\n    if (idx < targetIdx) return stop;\\n    if (idx === targetIdx) {\\n      return {\\n        ...stop,\\n        arrivalDate: newArrivalDate,\\n        departureDate: resolvedDeparture,\\n        stayNights,\\n      };\\n    }\\n    return {\\n      ...stop,\\n      arrivalDate: addDaysIso(stop.arrivalDate, departureDelta),\\n      departureDate: addDaysIso(stop.departureDate, departureDelta),\\n    };\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Updates stayNights for one stop (+/- nights) and cascades subsequent stops\' dates.\\n */\\nexport function updateStopNightsAndCascade(\\n  stops: TripStop[],\\n  targetStopId: string,\\n  deltaNights: number\\n): TripStop[] {\\n  const target = stops.find((s) => s.id === targetStopId);\\n  if (!target) return stops;\\n  const nextNights = Math.max(1, target.stayNights + deltaNights);\\n  const nextDeparture = addDaysIso(target.arrivalDate, nextNights);\\n  return updateStopDatesAndCascade(stops, targetStopId, target.arrivalDate, nextDeparture);\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Recalculates sequential arrival/departure dates across all stops after drag-and-drop\\n * reordering, anchoring on the earliest trip start date and preserving each stop\'s stayNights.\\n */\\nexport function recalculateDatesAfterReorder(\\n  reorderedStops: TripStop[],\\n  legs?: TripLeg[]\\n): TripStop[] {\\n  if (reorderedStops.length === 0) return reorderedStops;\\n\\n  // Anchor trip start date to the earliest existing arrival date so trip stays in its planned window\\n  const anchorStart = reorderedStops.reduce(\\n    (minDate, s) => (s.arrivalDate < minDate ? s.arrivalDate : minDate),\\n    reorderedStops[0].arrivalDate\\n  );\\n\\n  let cursorDate = anchorStart;\\n  return reorderedStops.map((stop, idx) => {\\n    if (idx > 0 && legs && legs[idx - 1]) {\\n      const leg = legs[idx - 1];\\n      const selected =\\n        leg.transitOptions.find((o) => o.id === leg.selectedOptionId) ??\\n        leg.transitOptions[0];\\n      // Add +1 calendar day when crossing long-haul overnight corridors (>= 9h)\\n      if (selected && selected.inVehicleHours + selected.layoverHours >= 9) {\\n        cursorDate = addDaysIso(cursorDate, 1);\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n    const nights = Math.max(1, stop.stayNights);\\n    const arrivalDate = cursorDate;\\n    const departureDate = addDaysIso(arrivalDate, nights);\\n    cursorDate = departureDate;\\n\\n    return {\\n      ...stop,\\n      order: idx + 1,\\n      arrivalDate,\\n      departureDate,\\n    };\\n  });\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Assigns Sunset Orange (#FF812E) to the currently selected stop,\\n * followed by Teal, Purple, Amber for remaining stops.\\n */\\nexport function getStopColorMap(\\n  stops: TripStop[],\\n  selectedStopId: string | null\\n): Record<string, string> {\\n  const map: Record<string, string> = {};\\n  const secondaryPalette = STOP_BADGE_PALETTE.slice(1);\\n  let secondaryIdx = 0;\\n\\n  for (const stop of stops) {\\n    if (stop.id === selectedStopId) {\\n      map[stop.id] = STOP_BADGE_PALETTE[0]; // #FF812E\\n    } else {\\n      map[stop.id] = secondaryPalette[secondaryIdx % secondaryPalette.length];\\n      secondaryIdx += 1;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  return map;\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Create UTC-safe date utility functions for two-way multi-destination date cascading and color-coded stop palette mapping.\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/shared/dateUtils.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating UTC date cascade and color utilities\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create shared/dateUtils.ts\"}"
