  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\nWe are building **Astris Travel**, a multi-destination travel planning and route optimization web application running as a live React + Vite + Express TypeScript workspace on port 3000 alongside FastAPI/Pydantic v2 and PostgreSQL reference deliverables.\n\nCurrent active user request (in progress): Add an interactive, color-coded **Multi-Destination Date Picker** modal/popover that syncs two-way with each stop\'s `arrivalDate`, `departureDate`, and `stayNights`:\n1. **Visual Design (Astris Light Theme):** Crisp white floating card (`bg-white border border-slate-200/80 shadow-xl rounded-2xl`), `Plus Jakarta Sans` (`font-display`) for month headers, `JetBrains Mono` (`font-mono tabular-nums`) for day numbers, NO dark background. Triggered from the date badge on any destination stop card or a trip-level date button in the summary bar.\n2. **Color-Coded City Highlights & Legend:** Assign Sunset Orange `#FF812E` to the currently selected stop, followed by Teal `#0D9488`, Purple `#7C3AED`, and Amber `#D97706`. Render booked nights across the calendar as circular/pill highlights with a horizontal color-dot city legend at the bottom.\n3. **Two-Way State Synchronization:**\n   - *Calendar \342\206\222 Timeline:* Selecting start and end dates updates `arrivalDate`, `departureDate`, and `stayNights` and cascades subsequent stops\' dates.\n   - *Timeline \342\206\222 Calendar:* Adjusting `- 3n +` or dragging stops into a new order immediately recalculates all stop dates and updates the calendar.\n\nResolved Phase 1 decisions & prior user directives:\n- **Runtime:** Live React + Vite + Express app on port 3000 + Python FastAPI/Pydantic v2 models (`/backend`) + PostgreSQL `SCHEMA.sql`.\n- **Map:** Token-free MapLibre GL (`react-map-gl/maplibre`) + `@turf/great-circle` over OpenFreeMap Positron (`https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/positron`) with OSM raster fallback.\n- **Brand Palette:** Sunset Orange `#FF812E` (hover `#E56B1A`, active tint `#FFF4ED`, border `#FFD6BA`), crisp white `#FFFFFF` cards over `#FAFAFA`, `#111827` primary text/prices, `#4B5563` secondary metadata.\n- **Smart Score VTTS Model:** 3-tier presets (`Budget Backpacker` `$5/hr`, `Balanced Explorer` `$15/hr` default, `Time-Rich / Express` `$35/hr`) + optional advanced slider, weighted by `modeMultiplier` (`0.4x` overnight sleeper, `1.0x` standard) and `layoverMultiplier` (`<2h: 1.0x`, `2\342\200\2235.99h: 1.5x`, `6+h: 2.5x`).\n- **UI Cleanliness:** High-density SaaS layout without helper blurbs, tutorial paragraphs, or verbose prose.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n**Completed Prior Deliverables:**\n- Installed packages: `@dnd-kit/core`, `@dnd-kit/sortable`, `@dnd-kit/utilities`, `maplibre-gl` (v6.18.0), `react-map-gl` (v8.1.3), `@turf/great-circle`, `@turf/helpers`.\n- Updated `/package.json` (`\"dev\": \"tsx server.ts\"`, `\"start\": \"node server.ts\"`), `/metadata.json`, `/index.html` (Google Fonts: `Plus Jakarta Sans`, `DM Sans`, `JetBrains Mono`), and `/src/index.css`.\n- Created `/shared/types.ts` (including `UserProfile`, `TransitSegment`, `TransitOption`, `TripStop`, `TripLeg`, `Voucher`, `Trip`, `RouteOptimizationResult`, `VoucherValidationResult`, `ferry` mode), `/shared/smartScore.ts` (weighted VTTS engine, `synthesizeCorridorOptions`, `buildLegsFromStops`), and `/shared/mockDataset.ts` (4-stop `Kuala Lumpur -> Istanbul -> London -> Paris` dataset with multi-segment `segments` and waypoints, `VOUCHERS_CATALOG`, `DESTINATION_HUBS`).\n- Created `/backend/`: `requirements.txt`, `SCHEMA.sql` (5 PostgreSQL tables: `users`, `trips`, `trip_legs`, `transit_options`, `vouchers` + indexes), `database.py`, `models.py` (Pydantic v2 aligned with `SCHEMA.sql`), `smart_score.py`, `main.py`, and `data/mock_trip.json`.\n- Created `/server.ts` serving Vite middleware in dev (`dist` in prod) + `/api/trips/default`, `/api/destinations`, `/api/vouchers`, `/api/legs/recompute`, `/api/optimize-route`, `/api/vouchers/validate`.\n- Created & streamlined UI components: `/src/components/TopBar.tsx`, `/src/components/VttsControlPanel.tsx`, `/src/components/LegTransitPanel.tsx`, `/src/components/AddStopModal.tsx`, `/src/components/RouteOptimizerModal.tsx`, `/src/components/VoucherDrawer.tsx`, `/src/components/WorldMapCanvas.tsx` (Rome2Rio mode-colored flight/train/bus polylines, junction nodes, directional plane icons, floating map callout pills, OpenFreeMap Positron style, `workerUrl` fix).\n- Created implementation plan artifact at `/.aistudio/artifacts/brain/fb7c045e-904d-498c-ad70-52c85fbc80f0/implementation_plan.md`.\n- Skills read earlier: `/skills/system_skills/planning_mode/SKILL.md`, `/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/SKILL.md`, `/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/references/3_saas_dashboard.md`.\n\n**Completed in Current Subtask (Multi-Destination Date Picker):**\n- Created `/shared/dateUtils.ts` with UTC-safe ISO date helpers (`parseIsoUtc`, `formatIsoUtc`, `addDaysIso`, `diffDaysIso`, `formatShortDate`, `formatTripDateSpan`), two-way cascading helpers (`updateStopDatesAndCascade`, `updateStopNightsAndCascade`, `recalculateDatesAfterReorder`), and `getStopColorMap` (`#FF812E` for selected stop, `#0D9488`, `#7C3AED`, `#D97706`, `#0284C7`, `#E11D48`).\n- Created `/src/components/MultiDestDatePickerModal.tsx` implementing the crisp white `rounded-2xl` modal, `Plus Jakarta Sans` month header, `JetBrains Mono` day grid, stop selector tabs, range selection + hover preview, color-coded pill highlights, and horizontal color-dot legend.\n\n**In Progress / Not Yet Wired:**\n- `/src/components/SortableStopCard.tsx` (read at lines 1\342\200\223134; not yet modified to accept `onOpenDatePicker` or `badgeColor` or make its date badge clickable).\n- `/src/App.tsx` (read at lines 200\342\200\223420; not yet modified to mount `MultiDestDatePickerModal`, add a trip-level date range button in the summary bar/header, or wire `updateStopDatesAndCascade`, `updateStopNightsAndCascade`, and `recalculateDatesAfterReorder` into `handleDragEnd`, `handleUpdateNights`, `handleAddDestination`, `handleRemoveStop`, and `handleApplyOptimized`).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n- **`maplibre-gl` v6.18.0 + Vite 8 Worker Behavior:** `maplibre-gl` exports named functions only (no default export) and defaults its worker URL relative to `import.meta.url`, which breaks inside `node_modules/.vite/deps/`. Passing `workerUrl={maplibreWorkerUrl}` from `import maplibreWorkerUrl from \'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl-worker.mjs?url\'` directly to `<Map>` (and calling `setWorkerUrl(maplibreWorkerUrl)`) works in both Vite dev (`/node_modules/maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl-worker.mjs`, 200 OK `text/javascript`) and `vite build` (`dist/assets/maplibre-gl-worker-*.mjs`).\n- **`DISABLE_HMR=true`:** Vite config sets `watch: null`, so running `restart_dev_server` is required after edits for the live preview server on port 3000 to reflect source changes.\n- **Basemap:** `https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/positron` returns HTTP 200 with zero API key watermarks.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n1. **`TS2741` / `TS1117` in `shared/smartScore.ts`:** Typo `toLng: toAirportLng` instead of `fromLng: toAirportLng` on synthesized segment 3. **Fixed** via `replace_file_content`.\n2. **`maplibre-gl` Worker Error (`Worker failed to load. Check that the worker URL is correct.`):** Caused by Vite pre-bundling `maplibre-gl` into `.vite/deps/` without `maplibre-gl-worker.mjs`. Attempted default import `import maplibregl from \'maplibre-gl\'` which failed `vite build` (`[MISSING_EXPORT] \"default\" is not exported`) and `tsc` (`TS1192`). **Fixed** by switching to `import { setWorkerUrl } from \'maplibre-gl\'`, importing `maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl-worker.mjs?url`, and passing `workerUrl={maplibreWorkerUrl}` to `<Map>` in `src/components/WorldMapCanvas.tsx` (also verified `react-map-gl` v8 `GlobalSettings.workerUrl` in `node_modules/@vis.gl/react-maplibre/dist/utils/set-globals.d.ts`).\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- Dev server is running on port 3000 via `tsx server.ts` (`restart_dev_server` should be called after completing the remaining edits).\n- Note on `MultiDestDatePickerModal.tsx`: Check `initialStopId` vs `stops` in the `useEffect` (`[isOpen, initialStopId, stops]`): when `stops` updates *while* the modal is open (e.g., user clicks dates inside the modal and `onUpdateStopDates` updates `stops`), `[isOpen, initialStopId, stops]` will re-run `setSelectedStopId(initialStopId ?? stops[0]?.id ?? \'\')`, which would reset `selectedStopId` back to `initialStopId` if the user switched stop tabs inside the modal! **Fix that `useEffect` dependency** so it only resets `selectedStopId` and `viewMonth` when `isOpen` transitions to `true` or `initialStopId` changes (remove `stops` from that `useEffect` dependency array or guard with `isOpen` transition).\n- Also check `recalculateDatesAfterReorder` in `/shared/dateUtils.ts`: in `handleDragEnd`, we should build/pass the new legs or compute dates cleanly after reordering, and ensure `handleAddDestination` / `handleRemoveStop` also keep `stops` dates sequential cleanly using UTC helpers (`addDaysIso`) instead of local `new Date()`.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Next Steps\n1. **Fix `useEffect` in `/src/components/MultiDestDatePickerModal.tsx`:** View lines 60\342\200\22380 and update the `useEffect` dependency array so changing `stops` while the modal is open preserves the currently selected stop tab inside the modal (only initialize `selectedStopId` and `viewMonth` when `isOpen` opens / `initialStopId` changes).\n2. **Update `/src/components/SortableStopCard.tsx`:**\n   - Add `badgeColor?: string` and `onOpenDatePicker: (stopId: string) => void` props.\n   - Replace the static `{stop.arrivalDate} \342\206\222 {stop.departureDate}` span with a clickable date badge/button (`onClick={() => onOpenDatePicker(stop.id)}`) featuring a `Calendar` icon (`w-3 h-3`) and crisp light hover styling (`rounded-lg px-2 py-0.5 border border-neutral-200/80 bg-neutral-50 hover:bg-[#FFF4ED] hover:border-[#FFD6BA]`). Optionally tint the stop\'s numbered badge or subtle dot indicator cleanly if helpful while keeping `#FF812E` prominent.\n3. **Update `/src/App.tsx`:**\n   - Import `MultiDestDatePickerModal` from `./components/MultiDestDatePickerModal.tsx` and `formatTripDateSpan`, `recalculateDatesAfterReorder`, `updateStopDatesAndCascade`, `updateStopNightsAndCascade`, `addDaysIso` from `../shared/dateUtils.ts`.\n   - Add state `datePickerStopId` (`string | null`) and `isDatePickerOpen` (`boolean`).\n   - Add a **trip-level date button** in the trip header / summary bar (near `Add Stop` & `Vouchers`, displaying `<Calendar />` + `formatTripDateSpan(trip.stops)`) that opens the modal with `trip.stops[0]?.id ?? null`.\n   - Implement `handleUpdateStopDates(stopId, arrivalDate, departureDate)` using `updateStopDatesAndCascade`, updating `trip.stops` cleanly (and keeping `legs` synced).\n   - Update `handleUpdateNights(stopId, delta)` to use `updateStopNightsAndCascade(prev.stops, stopId, delta)` so `- 3n +` immediately shifts `departureDate` and subsequent stops.\n   - Update `handleDragEnd` so `reordered = recalculateDatesAfterReorder(arrayMove(trip.stops, oldIndex, newIndex), ...)` recalculates all dates sequentially and passes the updated stops to `recomputeStopsAndLegs`. (Also ensure `handleRemoveStop` and `handleAddDestination` use UTC `addDaysIso` / `recalculateDatesAfterReorder` cleanly.)\n   - Pass `onOpenDatePicker` to `SortableStopCard` and render `<MultiDestDatePickerModal />`.\n4. **Verify & Restart:**\n   - Co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` together. Fix any issues if reported.\n   - Call `restart_dev_server` so the running port 3000 app serves the latest bundle.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Follow all `frontend-design` anti-slop rules: zero static pill badge clutter on metadata, clean `\302\267`/`/` separators, `tabular-nums` for numbers/dates, single-elevation `rounded-2xl` cards, no thick `border-l-4` borders, no dark calendar backgrounds, no explanatory tutorial paragraphs.\n- Keep `TopBar` strictly 3 zones (`Astris Travel` \342\200\224 nav links \342\200\224 `Optimize Route`).\n- Do NOT call `compile_applet` or `restart_dev_server` until edits are complete; on final verification, co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` together in one turn, then restart dev server.\n- Never leak internal file paths unnecessarily in the final user summary unless concise and helpful; keep summary crisp and factual.\n</summary>"
