      text: "Here is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.3.3\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^6.1.1\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^8.3.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\n@types/react: ^19.3.0\n@types/react-dom: ^19.3.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.3.3\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ^7.0.2\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(<App />);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  },\n  \"exclude\": [\"dist\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\342\200\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Act as a Principal Full-Stack Software Architect and UI/UX Engineer. We are building \"Astris Travel\", a global multi-destination travel planning and booking platform.\n\n### Design System & Visual Vibe (Crucial)\n- **Aesthetic:** Modern travel-tech (clean, airy, trustworthy, similar to Airbnb meets Wanderlog).\n- **Color Palette:** \n  - Backgrounds: Clean white and off-white (`bg-slate-50`).\n  - Text & Headers: Deep midnight slate (`text-slate-900` / `text-slate-600`).\n  - Accent & CTAs: Vibrant electric indigo (`bg-indigo-600 hover:bg-indigo-700 text-white`).\n  - Cards & Borders: Rounded corners (`rounded-2xl`), subtle border (`border border-slate-200/80`), and soft shadows (`shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all`).\n- **Layout:** Split-screen master workspace. \n  - **Left side:** Interactive drag-and-drop timeline/itinerary where users add and reorder destination stops.\n  - **Right side:** Interactive world map (Mapbox GL) with numbered pins (1, 2, 3...) and curved geodesic flight arcs connecting the legs, synchronized with timeline hover states.\n  - **Glassmorphism:** Floating transport filter bars over the map must use glassmorphism (`bg-white/80 backdrop-blur-md border border-white/20 shadow-lg rounded-full`).\n\n### Core Features to Build\n1. **Multi-Destination Timeline & Map Sync:** Sync reordering of stops on the timeline instantly with map coordinates and arc rendering.\n2. **Multi-Modal Routing:** Compare flights, trains, and buses door-to-door.\n3. **\"Smart Score\" Optimization:** Rank routes using a time-vs-price penalty algorithm (`Price + (Travel/Layover Hours \303\227 Hourly Time Value)`).\n4. **Two-Stage Global Route Optimizer:** Stage 1 filters geographical order locally; Stage 2 queries live transit APIs for top paths.\n5. **Voucher & Promo Engine:** Match active discount codes to eligible transit options.\n\n### Tech Stack\n- **Frontend:** Next.js (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, `@dnd-kit/core`, `react-map-gl` + `mapbox-gl` + `@turf/great-circle`.\n- **Backend:** Python (FastAPI) with Pydantic v2.\n- **Database & Cache:** PostgreSQL (Supabase) + Upstash Redis.\n- **APIs:** FlightPowers / SerpApi (flights) & Distribusion / Rome2Rio (ground transit).\n\n### Step 1 Deliverable\nGenerate the initial monorepo structure (`/frontend` and `/backend`), define the shared TypeScript and Pydantic models for `Trip`, `TripLeg` (with lat/lng), `TransitOption` (with smart score), and `Voucher`, and provide a realistic JSON mock dataset for a 4-stop trip (`Kuala Lumpur -> Istanbul -> London -> Paris`) so we can build the UI visually before hooking up live APIs.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nInstructions: If you need more context from the user you must first ask the user some questions using the ask_question tool. If you ask questions, you must wait for the user\'s answers. After the questions you must present a plan.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "<clarifying-answers>\nQ: This workspace runs React + Vite + Express on port 3000. How should we structure Astris Travel so your preview works immediately?\nA: Live React + Express app with FastAPI/Pydantic models\nQ: Mapbox GL requires a private access token to load map tiles. Which mapping setup do you prefer for the interactive world map?\nA: Token-free MapLibre GL with great-circle arcs\nQ: For this build, how complete should the interactive timeline, Smart Score engine, and voucher matcher be?\nA: Full interactive split-screen workspace with mock dataset\nQ: How should trip data and transit options be stored in this initial phase?\nA: Mock dataset + Express API endpoints first\n</clarifying-answers>"
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Update the Smart Score algorithm and UI controls in the implementation plan to use a realistic, tiered Value of Travel Time Savings (VTTS) model with pain multipliers:\n\n1. **UI Preset Toggle + Slider:** Replace the raw hourly slider with a 3-tier preset toggle (\"Budget Backpacker\" = $5/hr, \"Balanced Explorer\" = $15/hr default, \"Time-Rich / Express\" = $35/hr), while allowing optional fine-tuning via an advanced slider.\n2. **Weighted Smart Score Formula:** Instead of multiplying total hours by a flat hourly rate, weight each travel phase by its comfort/pain multiplier:\n   - In-vehicle travel (flight/train/bus): `1.0x` base rate (`0.4x` if overnight sleeper)\n   - Normal layover (2\342\200\2235 hours): `1.5x` base rate\n   - Long/painful layover (6+ hours): `2.5x` base rate\n   - Formula: `smartScore = discountedPrice + (inVehicleHours * baseRate * modeMultiplier) + (layoverHours * baseRate * layoverMultiplier)`\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nPlan action: revise\nPlan path: .aistudio/artifacts/brain/fb7c045e-904d-498c-ad70-52c85fbc80f0/implementation_plan.md\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Update the Design System and color palette in the implementation plan to use vibrant Sunset Orange (`#FF812E`) and crisp White as the primary brand identity, replacing the indigo accent colors:\n\n- **Primary Hero & Accent Color:** `#FF812E` (hover state: `#E56B1A`, soft tint background for active cards/badges: `#FFF4ED` with `#FFD6BA` border).\n- **Canvas & Card Backgrounds:** Pure crisp white (`#FFFFFF`) for cards, floating glassmorphic panels (`bg-white/85 backdrop-blur-md`), and modals, layered over a clean warm-neutral off-white workspace (`#FAFAFA`).\n- **Typography:** Deep charcoal (`#111827`) for primary headers and prices for high contrast, and neutral slate (`#4B5563`) for secondary metadata.\n- **Map Styling:** Render the numbered destination pins and primary active flight/transit arcs in `#FF812E` (with a soft white halo/outline on the map pins so they pop clearly against the map tiles).\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nPlan action: revise\nPlan path: .aistudio/artifacts/brain/fb7c045e-904d-498c-ad70-52c85fbc80f0/implementation_plan.md\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "The implementation plan looks great. Please proceed with building the full interactive application code based on this plan. Generate the components, mock data, and API structure now."
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Before we go further, please also incorporate this PostgreSQL database schema (`SCHEMA.sql`) into the architecture and backend files so it\'s ready when we connect persistence later:\n\n-- Enable UUID extension\nCREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS \"uuid-ossp\";\n\n-- 1. Users Table\nCREATE TABLE users (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),\n    email VARCHAR(255) UNIQUE NOT NULL,\n    full_name VARCHAR(100),\n    preferred_currency VARCHAR(3) DEFAULT \'USD\',\n    time_value_per_hour DECIMAL(6, 2) DEFAULT 15.00, -- Used for Smart Score penalty math\n    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n);\n\n-- 2. Trips Table\nCREATE TABLE trips (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),\n    user_id UUID REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    title VARCHAR(150) NOT NULL,\n    start_date DATE NOT NULL,\n    end_date DATE NOT NULL,\n    currency VARCHAR(3) DEFAULT \'USD\',\n    is_route_optimized BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE,\n    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n);\n\n-- 3. Trip Legs Table (Timeline stops + Map Coordinates)\nCREATE TABLE trip_legs (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),\n    trip_id UUID REFERENCES trips(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    order_index INT NOT NULL, -- Sequence on timeline & numbered map pin (1, 2, 3...)\n    \n    -- Origin Stop Details\n    origin_city VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,\n    origin_code VARCHAR(10) NOT NULL, -- e.g., KUL\n    origin_lat DECIMAL(9, 6) NOT NULL,\n    origin_lng DECIMAL(9, 6) NOT NULL,\n    \n    -- Destination Stop Details\n    destination_city VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,\n    destination_code VARCHAR(10) NOT NULL, -- e.g., IST\n    destination_lat DECIMAL(9, 6) NOT NULL,\n    destination_lng DECIMAL(9, 6) NOT NULL,\n    \n    -- Timing & Selection\n    departure_date DATE NOT NULL,\n    nights_at_destination INT DEFAULT 3,\n    selected_option_id UUID, -- References chosen TransitOption\n    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n);\n\n-- 4. Cached Transit Options (Flights, Trains, Buses, Ferries)\nCREATE TABLE transit_options (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),\n    leg_id UUID REFERENCES trip_legs(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n    transport_mode VARCHAR(20) CHECK (transport_mode IN (\'flight\', \'train\', \'bus\', \'ferry\')),\n    provider_name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL, -- e.g., Turkish Airlines, Eurostar\n    \n    -- Pricing & Vouchers\n    base_price DECIMAL(10, 2) NOT NULL,\n    discounted_price DECIMAL(10, 2),\n    applied_voucher_id UUID,\n    currency VARCHAR(3) DEFAULT \'USD\',\n    \n    -- Duration & Smart Score\n    departure_time TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE NOT NULL,\n    arrival_time TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE NOT NULL,\n    duration_minutes INT NOT NULL,\n    layover_minutes INT DEFAULT 0,\n    stops_count INT DEFAULT 0,\n    smart_score DECIMAL(10, 2) NOT NULL, -- Lower is better: price + (hours * time_value)\n    \n    -- Booking & Cache TTL\n    booking_url TEXT NOT NULL,\n    raw_api_payload JSONB,\n    expires_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE NOT NULL,\n    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n);\n\n-- 5. Vouchers & Discounts Table\nCREATE TABLE vouchers (\n    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),\n    provider_name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,\n    platform_source VARCHAR(100), -- e.g., Trip.com, Klook, Direct\n    promo_code VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,\n    description TEXT,\n    discount_type VARCHAR(20) CHECK (discount_type IN (\'percentage\', \'fixed\')),\n    discount_value DECIMAL(10, 2) NOT NULL,\n    max_discount_cap DECIMAL(10, 2),\n    min_spend DECIMAL(10, 2) DEFAULT 0.00,\n    valid_from DATE,\n    valid_until DATE,\n    is_active BOOLEAN DEFAULT TRUE,\n    created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n);\n\n-- Foreign Key Constraints\nALTER TABLE trip_legs \n    ADD CONSTRAINT fk_selected_option \n    FOREIGN KEY (selected_option_id) REFERENCES transit_options(id) ON DELETE SET NULL;\n\nALTER TABLE transit_options \n    ADD CONSTRAINT fk_applied_voucher \n    FOREIGN KEY (applied_voucher_id) REFERENCES vouchers(id) ON DELETE SET NULL;\n\n-- Performance Indexes\nCREATE INDEX idx_trip_legs_trip_order ON trip_legs(trip_id, order_index);\nCREATE INDEX idx_transit_options_leg_score ON transit_options(leg_id, smart_score ASC);\nCREATE INDEX idx_vouchers_active_provider ON vouchers(provider_name, is_active);"
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Please perform the following UI cleanup, map tile fix, and Rome2Rio-style multi-modal map upgrade across our React components and MapLibre workspace:\n\n### 1. UI Text Audit & Cleanup\n- Audit all dashboard, timeline, and card components and remove all unnecessary descriptive text, tutorial blurbs, helper paragraphs, and instructional sentences (e.g., remove \"Drag stops by the grip handle...\", VTTS explanations, etc.).\n- Keep only essential labels, telemetry numbers, status badges, and interactive controls for a clean, high-density SaaS layout.\n\n### 2. Fix Map Basemap (Remove Watermarks)\n- Replace the broken Carto basemap style URL (which currently renders \"API KEY REQUIRED\" watermarks) with a clean, token-free MapLibre basemap style (such as OpenFreeMap `https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/positron` or clean OSM raster tiles) so the world map renders crisply with zero watermarks.\n\n### 3. Rome2Rio-Style Multi-Modal Lines, Sub-Segments & Floating Callouts\nUpgrade `MapWorkspace` so every trip leg renders detailed, mode-distinct routing between nodes:\n- **Multi-Segment Door-to-Door Paths:** Support chaining sub-segments per leg (e.g., local airport rail transfer \342\206\222 main flight \342\206\222 arrival transit) with small white-bordered junction nodes (`8px` circles with white stroke) at transfer points.\n- **Mode-Specific Line Colors & Geometry:**\n  - **Flights:** Smooth, sweeping spherical great-circle arcs (`@turf/great-circle`) rendered in **Sunset Orange (`#FF812E`)**, `3px` width, with a directional airplane marker/icon along the arc.\n  - **Trains:** Road/rail-following multi-point GeoJSON polylines rendered in **Emerald/Teal (`#0D9488`)** with intermediate station dots along the path.\n  - **Buses & Local Transfers:** Multi-point ground polylines rendered in **Royal Purple (`#7C3AED`)** with intermediate stop dots.\n- **Floating White Callout Pills on Map:** Render compact, glassmorphic/white floating callout cards (`bg-white/95 backdrop-blur-sm shadow-md rounded-xl px-2.5 py-1.5 border border-slate-200/80`) anchored near key hubs/legs displaying:\n  - Step/Leg number, color-coded transport icon (plane/train/bus), hub/city name, and duration (e.g., `1 \360\237\232\206 KLIA Ekspres \302\267 32m` or `2 \342\234\210\357\270\217 Istanbul (IST) \302\267 11h 12m`)."
    }
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Fix the errors in the app\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nfix_it_trigger: manual\nerror 0: Error: Worker failed to load. Check that the worker URL is correct.\n    at Worker.<anonymous> (https://ais-dev-weoarravs43cujy4bu3a3l-61961924567.asia-southeast1.run.app/node_modules/.vite/deps/maplibre-gl-DsifqegG.js?v=9d30d367:9439:32)\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
