    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Add an interactive, color-coded Multi-Destination Date Picker popover/modal that syncs directly with each stop\'s `arrivalDate`, `departureDate`, and `stayNights`:\n\n### 1. Visual Design (Astris Light Theme)\n- Style the calendar container as a crisp white floating popover/card (`bg-white border border-slate-200/80 shadow-xl rounded-2xl`) using `Plus Jakarta Sans` for the month header and `JetBrains Mono` (`tabular-nums`) for day numbers\342\200\224do NOT use a dark background.\n- Trigger the calendar when clicking the date badge on any destination stop card or a trip-level date button in the summary bar.\n\n### 2. Color-Coded City Highlights & Legend\n- Assign each stop in the itinerary a distinct, accessible badge color (starting with Sunset Orange `#FF812E` for the currently selected stop, followed by Teal `#0D9488`, Purple `#7C3AED`, and Amber `#D97706`).\n- Render each city\'s booked nights as circular/pill highlights across the calendar dates, and display a clean horizontal color-dot legend at the bottom of the calendar mapping each color to its city name (e.g., `\342\227\217 Paris`, `\342\227\217 Istanbul`).\n\n### 3. Two-Way State Synchronization\n- **Calendar \342\206\222 Timeline:** Selecting a start and end date for a destination updates that stop\'s `arrivalDate`, `departureDate`, and `stayNights`, and automatically cascades/shifts the dates of subsequent stops in the sequence.\n- **Timeline \342\206\222 Calendar:** Adjusting a stop\'s night counter (`- 3n +`) or dragging stops into a new order immediately recalculates all stop dates and updates the colored blocks on the calendar."
    }
  }
}
