  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing The Edits**\n\nI\'m making swift progress. I understand the edit is in `/src/components/MultiDestDatePickerModal.tsx`, specifically lines 62-75. The `useEffect` hook\'s dependencies are resetting the `selectedStopId`. I\'ll review and cleanly address this.\n\n\n**Refining The Dependencies**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the dependency array issue. The `useEffect` hook\'s reliance on `stops` is the culprit, causing unwanted resets. My current plan is to synchronize `selectedStopId` and `viewMonth` only upon opening the calendar, or when the `initialStopId` changes. I will achieve this by utilizing a ref, ensuring the `useEffect` hook\'s dependencies are `[isOpen, initialStopId]` for cleaner, more predictable behavior, which mitigates warnings. I\'ll also ensure selected stops stay valid on external stop deletion.\n\n\n**Streamlining Date Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the date display and telemetry within the modal. I\'m streamlining the text in the modal to be concise and telemetry-focused. The text will now show the check-in and check-out dates, or `Select start \342\206\222 end`. I will also add `onOpenDatePicker` prop to `SortableStopCard.tsx` and evaluate UI implications.\n\n\n**Implementing Date Badges**\n\nI\'m now implementing interactive date badges within the stop cards. I\'m swapping the existing date display with a button that launches the date picker, improving the UI. I\'m adding distinct badge colors, starting with Sunset Orange, for visual distinction. I\'ve also integrated the `Calendar` icon and styled the badge button with inline flexbox for a crisp appearance. The metadata is still visible for clarity, but the dates are now represented by a concise, interactive element.\n\n\n**Adding Date Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating date manipulation functions from `dateUtils.ts` to manage stop dates. I\'ve added state variables for date picker visibility and the currently selected stop ID. I\'ve implemented a handler to open the date picker, focusing the UI on the targeted stop. Furthermore, I\'ve implemented handlers to update stop dates and nights, ensuring date changes cascade correctly and that the trip\'s start and end dates are properly synchronized.\n\n\n**Sequencing Drag and Drop**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the date recalculation within the drag-and-drop functionality. After a reorder event, I\'ll need to recalculate dates sequentially. I\'ve pinpointed `recalculateDatesAfterReorder` as the key function, and am integrating it directly into `handleDragEnd`. My current plan is to apply `recalculateDatesAfterReorder` to the reordered stops, ensuring that leg data updates accordingly.\n\n\n**Calculating Date Relationships**\n\nI\'m now focusing on date recalculation after stop removals and additions. I\'m going to ensure sequential dates are recomputed, avoiding gaps when stops are removed. Specifically, I\'ll integrate `recalculateDatesAfterReorder` and re-evaluate `setTrip` calls within `recomputeStopsAndLegs` to synchronize `startDate` and `endDate`. Furthermore, I will use `addDaysIso` from `dateUtils.ts` to add days for new destination arrivals, which will resolve timezone issues. I\'ll handle removing stops to ensure the reordering maintains sequential date continuity and prevent multi-day gaps. I\'ll need to compute `prelimLegs`, then `datedStops`, then `recomputeStopsAndLegs`!\n\n\n**Integrating Date Display**\n\nI\'ve tested the date recalculation after stop removals, ensuring a gap-free calendar via `recalculateDatesAfterReorder`. I\'ve added a trip-level date button to the summary bar in `App.tsx` (lines 468-486), and passed `onOpenDatePicker` to `<SortableStopCard />`. I\'ll render the `<MultiDestDatePickerModal />` in `App.tsx` now. The next step is to test the integration.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1087824621783608876"
      name: "multi_replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"Description\":\"Preserve active stop tab while open when stops update, and streamline status label\", \"Instruction\":\"Update useEffect with a ref for stops so changing dates inside the modal does not reset selectedStopId, and tighten footer status text\", \"ReplacementChunks\":[{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":2, \"ReplacementContent\":\"import { useEffect, useMemo, useRef, useState } from \'react\';\\nimport { Calendar, ChevronLeft, ChevronRight, X } from \'lucide-react\';\", \"StartLine\":1, \"TargetContent\":\"import { useEffect, useMemo, useState } from \'react\';\\nimport { Calendar, ChevronLeft, ChevronRight, X } from \'lucide-react\';\"}, {\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":75, \"ReplacementContent\":\"  const stopsRef = useRef(stops);\\n  stopsRef.current = stops;\\n\\n  // Sync active stop & visible month only when modal opens or initialStopId changes\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    if (!isOpen) return;\\n    const currentStops = stopsRef.current;\\n    const targetId = initialStopId ?? currentStops[0]?.id ?? \'\';\\n    setSelectedStopId(targetId);\\n    setDraftStartIso(null);\\n    setHoverIso(null);\\n    const targetStop = currentStops.find((s) => s.id === targetId) ?? currentStops[0];\\n    if (targetStop) {\\n      const dt = parseIsoUtc(targetStop.arrivalDate);\\n      setViewMonth({ year: dt.getUTCFullYear(), month: dt.getUTCMonth() });\\n    }\\n  }, [isOpen, initialStopId]);\", \"StartLine\":62, \"TargetContent\":\"  // Sync active stop & visible month when opened from a specific stop card\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    if (!isOpen) return;\\n    const targetId = initialStopId ?? stops[0]?.id ?? \'\';\\n    setSelectedStopId(targetId);\\n    setDraftStartIso(null);\\n    setHoverIso(null);\\n    const targetStop = stops.find((s) => s.id === targetId) ?? stops[0];\\n    if (targetStop) {\\n      const dt = parseIsoUtc(targetStop.arrivalDate);\\n      setViewMonth({ year: dt.getUTCFullYear(), month: dt.getUTCMonth() });\\n    }\\n  }, [isOpen, initialStopId, stops]);\"}, {\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":370, \"ReplacementContent\":\"                : activeStop\\n                  ? `${activeStop.city} \302\267 ${formatShortDate(activeStop.arrivalDate)} \342\206\222 ${formatShortDate(activeStop.departureDate)}`\\n                  : \'\'}\", \"StartLine\":367, \"TargetContent\":\"                : activeStop\\n                  ? `Editing ${activeStop.city} \302\267 Click start & end date`\\n                  : \'\'}\"}], \"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/MultiDestDatePickerModal.tsx\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating date picker modal\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update date picker modal\"}"
