  planner_response {
    response: "Implemented and wired the interactive, color-coded **Multi-Destination Date Picker** with two-way itinerary synchronization:\n\n- **Astris Light Calendar UI:** Built `MultiDestDatePickerModal` as a crisp white floating dialog (`bg-white border border-slate-200/80 shadow-xl rounded-2xl`) using `Plus Jakarta Sans` month headers and `JetBrains Mono` (`tabular-nums`) day cells, stop selector tabs, and hover-preview range selection.\n- **Color-Coded City Highlights & Legend:** Assigned Sunset Orange (`#FF812E`) to the active destination stop followed by Teal (`#0D9488`), Purple (`#7C3AED`), and Amber (`#D97706`), rendering each city\'s booked nights as continuous pill highlights with a horizontal color-dot legend at the bottom.\n- **Calendar & Timeline Triggers:** Added a trip-level date span button in the workspace summary bar (`formatTripDateSpan`) and made each stop card\'s date badge interactive so clicking either opens the calendar focused on that destination.\n- **Two-Way State Synchronization:**\n  - *Calendar \342\206\222 Timeline:* Selecting a start and end date updates `arrivalDate`, `departureDate`, and `stayNights` via UTC-safe helpers (`updateStopDatesAndCascade`) and shifts subsequent stops automatically.\n  - *Timeline \342\206\222 Calendar:* Adjusting `- 3n +` (`updateStopNightsAndCascade`), reordering stops via drag-and-drop (`recalculateDatesAfterReorder`), adding or removing stops, and applying route optimizations immediately recalculate sequential trip dates and update the calendar.\n\n**Verification:** `npm run build` (`compile_applet`) and `tsc --noEmit` (`lint_applet`) passed with zero errors, and the dev server was restarted cleanly."
    modified_response: "Implemented and wired the interactive, color-coded **Multi-Destination Date Picker** with two-way itinerary synchronization:\n\n- **Astris Light Calendar UI:** Built `MultiDestDatePickerModal` as a crisp white floating dialog (`bg-white border border-slate-200/80 shadow-xl rounded-2xl`) using `Plus Jakarta Sans` month headers and `JetBrains Mono` (`tabular-nums`) day cells, stop selector tabs, and hover-preview range selection.\n- **Color-Coded City Highlights & Legend:** Assigned Sunset Orange (`#FF812E`) to the active destination stop followed by Teal (`#0D9488`), Purple (`#7C3AED`), and Amber (`#D97706`), rendering each city\'s booked nights as continuous pill highlights with a horizontal color-dot legend at the bottom.\n- **Calendar & Timeline Triggers:** Added a trip-level date span button in the workspace summary bar (`formatTripDateSpan`) and made each stop card\'s date badge interactive so clicking either opens the calendar focused on that destination.\n- **Two-Way State Synchronization:**\n  - *Calendar \342\206\222 Timeline:* Selecting a start and end date updates `arrivalDate`, `departureDate`, and `stayNights` via UTC-safe helpers (`updateStopDatesAndCascade`) and shifts subsequent stops automatically.\n  - *Timeline \342\206\222 Calendar:* Adjusting `- 3n +` (`updateStopNightsAndCascade`), reordering stops via drag-and-drop (`recalculateDatesAfterReorder`), adding or removing stops, and applying route optimizations immediately recalculate sequential trip dates and update the calendar.\n\n**Verification:** `npm run build` (`compile_applet`) and `tsc --noEmit` (`lint_applet`) passed with zero errors, and the dev server was restarted cleanly."
