  user_input {
    user_response: "In the Itinerary Dates modal/popover, lock each destination\'s assigned color permanently so colors never swap when selecting different stops:\n\n### 1. Fixed Color Assignment per Stop\n- Assign each stop a permanent color based on its `stop.id` or initial sequence index (e.g., Stop 1 = Sunset Orange `#FF812E`, Stop 2 = Teal `#0D9488`, Stop 3 = Royal Purple `#7C3AED`, Stop 4 = Amber `#D97706`).\n- Do **not** override a stop\'s calendar highlight color or dot color with `#FF812E` when it becomes the active/selected stop.\n\n### 2. Visual Selection State Without Color Swapping\n- **Calendar Grid:** Keep each stop\'s date range pills and end-caps permanently rendered in that stop\'s assigned color (with a soft tinted fill for middle nights) regardless of which stop is currently active. Optionally add a subtle outer ring (`ring-2 ring-offset-1`) in that stop\'s own color around the currently active stop\'s dates.\n- **Top Destination Selector Tabs & Bottom Legend:** Keep the colored dot next to each city name permanently fixed to that city\'s assigned color. Indicate which city tab is currently selected using a crisp border, bold text, and a subtle neutral or matching-tint background\342\200\224never by changing its color dot to orange."
    items {
      text: "In the Itinerary Dates modal/popover, lock each destination\'s assigned color permanently so colors never swap when selecting different stops:\n\n### 1. Fixed Color Assignment per Stop\n- Assign each stop a permanent color based on its `stop.id` or initial sequence index (e.g., Stop 1 = Sunset Orange `#FF812E`, Stop 2 = Teal `#0D9488`, Stop 3 = Royal Purple `#7C3AED`, Stop 4 = Amber `#D97706`).\n- Do **not** override a stop\'s calendar highlight color or dot color with `#FF812E` when it becomes the active/selected stop.\n\n### 2. Visual Selection State Without Color Swapping\n- **Calendar Grid:** Keep each stop\'s date range pills and end-caps permanently rendered in that stop\'s assigned color (with a soft tinted fill for middle nights) regardless of which stop is currently active. Optionally add a subtle outer ring (`ring-2 ring-offset-1`) in that stop\'s own color around the currently active stop\'s dates.\n- **Top Destination Selector Tabs & Bottom Legend:** Keep the colored dot next to each city name permanently fixed to that city\'s assigned color. Indicate which city tab is currently selected using a crisp border, bold text, and a subtle neutral or matching-tint background\342\200\224never by changing its color dot to orange."
    }
