    model_api_content_id: "0181974c94f9408a808206b6f3efca0f"
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Fix the date overlapping bug and the horizontal clipping in the Itinerary Dates modal:\n\n### 1. Prevent Date Overlaps & Enforce Sequential Chaining\n- **Auto-Shift Subsequent Stops:** When a stop\'s `arrivalDate` or `departureDate` is modified, automatically cascade and shift all subsequent stops (`index > activeIndex`) forward so `nextStop.arrivalDate` always equals `currentStop.departureDate` (or later). Never allow two destinations to occupy the same night or overlap.\n- **Prevent Collision with Previous Stops:** Disable or clamp date selection earlier than the preceding stop\'s `departureDate` (or automatically adjust the preceding stop\'s `departureDate` / `stayNights` cleanly to match the new split point so `prevStop.departureDate === activeStop.arrivalDate` with zero overlap).\n- **Clean Checkout / Transit Day Rendering:** On transition days where Stop A departs and Stop B arrives on the same calendar date, render a clean split-pill or ensure the active stop\'s start cap doesn\'t collide awkwardly with the previous stop\'s end cap.\n\n### 2. Fix Top Pill Row Clipping & Scrollbar\n- In the top destination selector bar (`1. Kuala Lumpur`, `2. Istanbul`, `3. London`, `4. Paris`), replace the wide horizontal scrollbar with `flex-wrap gap-2` (or compact `px-2.5 py-1 text-xs` pills) so all 4 destination tabs fit cleanly inside the modal width without overflowing off the right edge.\n- Keep the bottom footer (`legend` on the left, `Done` button on the right) on a single aligned horizontal row (`flex items-center justify-between`)."
    items {
      text: "Fix the date overlapping bug and the horizontal clipping in the Itinerary Dates modal:\n\n### 1. Prevent Date Overlaps & Enforce Sequential Chaining\n- **Auto-Shift Subsequent Stops:** When a stop\'s `arrivalDate` or `departureDate` is modified, automatically cascade and shift all subsequent stops (`index > activeIndex`) forward so `nextStop.arrivalDate` always equals `currentStop.departureDate` (or later). Never allow two destinations to occupy the same night or overlap.\n- **Prevent Collision with Previous Stops:** Disable or clamp date selection earlier than the preceding stop\'s `departureDate` (or automatically adjust the preceding stop\'s `departureDate` / `stayNights` cleanly to match the new split point so `prevStop.departureDate === activeStop.arrivalDate` with zero overlap).\n- **Clean Checkout / Transit Day Rendering:** On transition days where Stop A departs and Stop B arrives on the same calendar date, render a clean split-pill or ensure the active stop\'s start cap doesn\'t collide awkwardly with the previous stop\'s end cap.\n\n### 2. Fix Top Pill Row Clipping & Scrollbar\n- In the top destination selector bar (`1. Kuala Lumpur`, `2. Istanbul`, `3. London`, `4. Paris`), replace the wide horizontal scrollbar with `flex-wrap gap-2` (or compact `px-2.5 py-1 text-xs` pills) so all 4 destination tabs fit cleanly inside the modal width without overflowing off the right edge.\n- Keep the bottom footer (`legend` on the left, `Done` button on the right) on a single aligned horizontal row (`flex items-center justify-between`)."
    }
  }
}
