  user_input {
    user_response: "Refactor the calendar date-cell rendering in the Itinerary Dates modal so the entire multi-city trip forms one continuous, seamless horizontal ribbon without intermediate rounded end-caps:\n\n### 1. Continuous Ribbon Border-Radius Rules\n- **Trip Start Date ONLY (First Stop\'s `arrivalDate`, e.g., Nov 2):** Render as a solid pill cap rounded **only on the left** (`rounded-l-full rounded-r-none`) in the first stop\'s primary color.\n- **Trip End Date ONLY (Last Stop\'s `departureDate`, e.g., Nov 22):** Render as a solid pill cap rounded **only on the right** (`rounded-r-full rounded-l-none`) in the last stop\'s primary color.\n- **All Other Dates (Intermediate Nights & Handoff Days):** Render strictly as **sharp-cornered rectangles (`rounded-none`)** with zero pill rounding on the left or right, even if a night falls on a Monday or Sunday edge of the calendar grid.\n\n### 2. Remove Intermediate Solid End-Caps\n- Do **not** render solid dark-colored end-caps on the night before a transition (e.g., remove the solid caps on Nov 4, Nov 9, and Nov 18).\n- Every regular night between the trip start date and trip end date should use that stop\'s **soft tinted background** (e.g., `bg-orange-50`, `bg-teal-50`, `bg-purple-50`, `bg-amber-50`) with crisp dark text (`text-slate-900`).\n\n### 3. Split-Color Rectangles for Handoff/Transition Days\n- On dates where one stop departs and the next stop arrives (e.g., Nov 5, Nov 10, Nov 19), render a **flat rectangle (`rounded-none`)** split diagonally (or vertically 50/50) between the outgoing stop\'s solid color and the incoming stop\'s solid color, with crisp white centered day text (`text-white font-semibold`).\n- Ensure the active selected stop\'s range highlight (if shown) wraps cleanly around the rectangular cells without adding rounded pill curves to middle days."
    items {
      text: "Refactor the calendar date-cell rendering in the Itinerary Dates modal so the entire multi-city trip forms one continuous, seamless horizontal ribbon without intermediate rounded end-caps:\n\n### 1. Continuous Ribbon Border-Radius Rules\n- **Trip Start Date ONLY (First Stop\'s `arrivalDate`, e.g., Nov 2):** Render as a solid pill cap rounded **only on the left** (`rounded-l-full rounded-r-none`) in the first stop\'s primary color.\n- **Trip End Date ONLY (Last Stop\'s `departureDate`, e.g., Nov 22):** Render as a solid pill cap rounded **only on the right** (`rounded-r-full rounded-l-none`) in the last stop\'s primary color.\n- **All Other Dates (Intermediate Nights & Handoff Days):** Render strictly as **sharp-cornered rectangles (`rounded-none`)** with zero pill rounding on the left or right, even if a night falls on a Monday or Sunday edge of the calendar grid.\n\n### 2. Remove Intermediate Solid End-Caps\n- Do **not** render solid dark-colored end-caps on the night before a transition (e.g., remove the solid caps on Nov 4, Nov 9, and Nov 18).\n- Every regular night between the trip start date and trip end date should use that stop\'s **soft tinted background** (e.g., `bg-orange-50`, `bg-teal-50`, `bg-purple-50`, `bg-amber-50`) with crisp dark text (`text-slate-900`).\n\n### 3. Split-Color Rectangles for Handoff/Transition Days\n- On dates where one stop departs and the next stop arrives (e.g., Nov 5, Nov 10, Nov 19), render a **flat rectangle (`rounded-none`)** split diagonally (or vertically 50/50) between the outgoing stop\'s solid color and the incoming stop\'s solid color, with crisp white centered day text (`text-white font-semibold`).\n- Ensure the active selected stop\'s range highlight (if shown) wraps cleanly around the rectangular cells without adding rounded pill curves to middle days."
    }
  }
}
