  user_input {
    user_response: "Update the Itinerary Dates calendar cell styling so that rounded front/end pill caps appear ONLY while actively selecting a date range, and automatically flatten into the continuous ribbon once the end date is confirmed:\n\n### 1. Active Selection State (`isSelectingRange === true` \342\200\224 after clicking start date, before clicking end date)\n- **Temporary Start & Hover End Pills:** While the user has picked a `pendingStartDate` for the selected destination and is hovering/choosing an end date:\n  - Render `pendingStartDate` with a **rounded left pill cap** (`rounded-l-full rounded-r-none`) in the selected stop\'s solid color.\n  - Render the hovered/prospective end date with a **rounded right pill cap** (`rounded-r-full rounded-l-none`) in the selected stop\'s solid color.\n  - Render all intermediate hovered dates between them as flat rectangles (`rounded-none`) with that stop\'s soft tinted background.\n- Meanwhile, keep all **non-selected** stops rendered in their normal flat/continuous ribbon state.\n\n### 2. Confirmed / Committed State (`isSelectingRange === false` \342\200\224 immediately upon clicking the end date)\n- The instant the user clicks their end date to confirm the range, **remove the temporary rounded pill caps** from the selected stop and snap the entire calendar back into the unified continuous ribbon:\n  - **Only** the very first date of the entire trip (Stop 1\'s `arrivalDate`, e.g., Nov 2) keeps a left pill cap (`rounded-l-full rounded-r-none`).\n  - **Only** the very last date of the entire trip (Last Stop\'s `departureDate`, e.g., Nov 18) keeps a right pill cap (`rounded-r-full rounded-l-none`).\n  - All transition/handoff days between stops (e.g., Nov 5, Nov 11, Nov 14) render as **sharp-cornered split-color rectangles (`rounded-none`)** with zero pill rounding.\n  - All other regular nights render as sharp-cornered tinted rectangles (`rounded-none`)."
    items {
      text: "Update the Itinerary Dates calendar cell styling so that rounded front/end pill caps appear ONLY while actively selecting a date range, and automatically flatten into the continuous ribbon once the end date is confirmed:\n\n### 1. Active Selection State (`isSelectingRange === true` \342\200\224 after clicking start date, before clicking end date)\n- **Temporary Start & Hover End Pills:** While the user has picked a `pendingStartDate` for the selected destination and is hovering/choosing an end date:\n  - Render `pendingStartDate` with a **rounded left pill cap** (`rounded-l-full rounded-r-none`) in the selected stop\'s solid color.\n  - Render the hovered/prospective end date with a **rounded right pill cap** (`rounded-r-full rounded-l-none`) in the selected stop\'s solid color.\n  - Render all intermediate hovered dates between them as flat rectangles (`rounded-none`) with that stop\'s soft tinted background.\n- Meanwhile, keep all **non-selected** stops rendered in their normal flat/continuous ribbon state.\n\n### 2. Confirmed / Committed State (`isSelectingRange === false` \342\200\224 immediately upon clicking the end date)\n- The instant the user clicks their end date to confirm the range, **remove the temporary rounded pill caps** from the selected stop and snap the entire calendar back into the unified continuous ribbon:\n  - **Only** the very first date of the entire trip (Stop 1\'s `arrivalDate`, e.g., Nov 2) keeps a left pill cap (`rounded-l-full rounded-r-none`).\n  - **Only** the very last date of the entire trip (Last Stop\'s `departureDate`, e.g., Nov 18) keeps a right pill cap (`rounded-r-full rounded-l-none`).\n  - All transition/handoff days between stops (e.g., Nov 5, Nov 11, Nov 14) render as **sharp-cornered split-color rectangles (`rounded-none`)** with zero pill rounding.\n  - All other regular nights render as sharp-cornered tinted rectangles (`rounded-none`)."
    }
  }
}
