  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Specific Requirements**\n\nI\'ve homed in on a concrete requirement. I\'m currently scrutinizing `/src/components/MultiDestDatePickerModal.tsx`, specifically lines 315\342\200\223415. The immediate focus is understanding the current behavior when `draftStartIso !== null`, effectively when `isSelectingRange === true`. This should give a good start.\n\n\n**Clarifying Hover States**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the hover state logic within the date picker component. My focus is on ensuring that the rounded pill cap styling is applied correctly, especially when a start date (`draftStartIso`) is selected, but an end date (`previewEndIso`) hasn\'t been chosen yet. The logic seems straightforward for the start date, always rounded-left. The end date logic also seems solid, always rounding on the right when `previewEndIso` is hovered. Now, I will double check the in-between state.\n\n\n**Investigating Date Picker States**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into how the date picker renders the selected date range. I\'m focusing on the visual states, specifically the rounded pill styling for dates during range selection when `draftStartIso` has a value but `previewEndIso` is still null. I\'m scrutinizing the conditional logic determining when to apply the rounded-left, rounded-right, and flat styles, especially how they interact with non-selected stops and draft states. I need to fully grasp how the component transitions between these states during range selection and final confirmation.\n\n\n**Confirming Visual Transitions**\n\nI\'ve been thinking about the instant visual transition when the user selects an end date, effectively ending the date range selection, and I think I understand the logic. The entire calendar resets to show a unified continuous ribbon. Now I need to confirm: Only the start date gets the left-rounded styling; only the end date gets the right-rounded styling; handoff days are flat-styled and split-colored; regular nights are flat and soft-tinted. Now I need to check the minor detail regarding `activeStop` and new start dates, like at lines 366-367.\n\n\n**Refining Conditional Logic**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the conditional styling logic, specifically how `isDraftStart` and `isDraftEnd` visually override other states. I\'m focusing on the user interaction flow from the initial start date selection, through hovering over potential end dates. I think I understand the logic that happens when a user clicks the start date, the states get reset, and the rendering logic updates the display. The hovering case is also clear. I will update lines 331-354.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_14675678292686950957"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Render rounded-l-full and rounded-r-full temporary pill caps on pending start and hovered end dates exclusively while isSelectingRange is active\", \"EndLine\":356, \"Instruction\":\"Update the isAnyDraft branch in MultiDestDatePickerModal so draftStartIso always renders rounded-l-full rounded-r-none and previewEndIso always renders rounded-r-full rounded-l-none during active range selection\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"              const isSelectingRange = draftStartIso !== null;\\n\\n              if (isAnyDraft && isSelectingRange) {\\n                if (isDraftStart) {\\n                  // Pending start date: temporary rounded left pill cap in active stop\'s solid color\\n                  bgStyle = activeColor;\\n                  textColor = \'#FFFFFF\';\\n                  fontWeightClass = \'font-bold\';\\n                  radiusClass = \'rounded-l-full rounded-r-none\';\\n                } else if (isDraftEnd) {\\n                  // Prospective hovered end date: temporary rounded right pill cap in active stop\'s solid color\\n                  bgStyle = activeColor;\\n                  textColor = \'#FFFFFF\';\\n                  fontWeightClass = \'font-bold\';\\n                  radiusClass = \'rounded-r-full rounded-l-none\';\\n                } else {\\n                  // Intermediate hovered nights: flat sharp-cornered soft-tinted rectangles\\n                  bgStyle = `${activeColor}26`;\\n                  textColor = \'#111827\';\\n                  fontWeightClass = \'font-semibold\';\\n                  radiusClass = \'rounded-none\';\\n                  boxShadowStyle = `inset 0 2px 0 0 ${activeColor}, inset 0 -2px 0 0 ${activeColor}`;\\n                }\\n              } else if (isTripStart) {\", \"StartLine\":326, \"TargetContent\":\"              if (isAnyDraft) {\\n                if (isDraftStart) {\\n                  bgStyle = activeColor;\\n                  textColor = \'#FFFFFF\';\\n                  fontWeightClass = \'font-bold\';\\n                  radiusClass =\\n                    activeStopIndex === 0 ? \'rounded-l-full rounded-r-none\' : \'rounded-none\';\\n                } else if (isDraftEnd) {\\n                  bgStyle = activeColor;\\n                  textColor = \'#FFFFFF\';\\n                  fontWeightClass = \'font-bold\';\\n                  radiusClass =\\n                    activeStopIndex === stops.length - 1\\n                      ? \'rounded-r-full rounded-l-none\'\\n                      : \'rounded-none\';\\n                } else {\\n                  bgStyle = `${activeColor}26`;\\n                  textColor = \'#111827\';\\n                  fontWeightClass = \'font-semibold\';\\n                  radiusClass = \'rounded-none\';\\n                  boxShadowStyle = `inset 0 2px 0 0 ${activeColor}, inset 0 -2px 0 0 ${activeColor}`;\\n                }\\n              } else if (isTripStart) {\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/MultiDestDatePickerModal.tsx\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating active range selection pills\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update active range selection pills\"}"
